WEBVTT

1
00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:48.542
- Straight?
- What? Oh, shit! Left!

2
00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:50.375
- Which left?
- The one we just passed.

3
00:02:50.542 --> 00:02:52.726
- Can you stop scrolling for five minutes?
- Why are you speeding like crazy?

4
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:53.667
Are you trying to catch a train
or something?

5
00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:54.893
- So this is my fault?
- Yeah, totally!

6
00:02:54.917 --> 00:02:56.757
I gave you one job,
and you still messed it up.

7
00:02:56.792 --> 00:02:58.434
If you want to keep scrolling
on Instagram, go sit in the back.

8
00:02:58.458 --> 00:02:59.500
Pihu, come sit here.

9
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:02.125
You've taken this route so many times.
How do you not remember?

10
00:03:02.208 --> 00:03:03.542
Am I your personal GPS?

11
00:03:41.958 --> 00:03:45.375
Shruti and I cherished
the madness we shared.

12
00:03:45.875 --> 00:03:48.083
We held the sky in our hands
and reveled in adventure.

13
00:03:49.375 --> 00:03:51.250
Nice one! Just jump.

14
00:03:52.625 --> 00:03:53.625
Good to go.

15
00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:58.917
I love you!

16
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.875
<i>All we wanted was
a carefree flight through life.</i>

17
00:04:02.458 --> 00:04:05.125
<i>But our families weren't cool
with our freedom.</i>

18
00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:10.750
Your dream to be a musician… gone!

19
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:13.000
Your freedom… gone!

20
00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.125
All your dreams… gone!

21
00:04:16.208 --> 00:04:17.125
<i>We got married.</i>

22
00:04:17.208 --> 00:04:19.417
Responsibilities pushed us
from Delhi to Bangalore.

23
00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.417
Then came the corporate job,
the tie, and a used car on EMI.

24
00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:26.250
I didn't even notice when the keyboard
replaced my guitar.

25
00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:32.875
<i>Why does life after marriage
Change so drastically?</i>

26
00:04:33.417 --> 00:04:34.583
<i>Even though we've changed…</i>

27
00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:38.042
<i>-Our love remains pure
-Our love</i>

28
00:04:38.125 --> 00:04:42.875
<i>-The rush, the madness, all the fun
-You and your crazy, still as one</i>

29
00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.333
Your obsession with
doing it out in the open

30
00:04:45.875 --> 00:04:47.309
is going to get us in trouble one day.

31
00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:49.601
But if we don't wrap ourselves
in the blanket of the stars above,

32
00:04:49.625 --> 00:04:51.792
how will we feel the heat, my love?

33
00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:56.625
<i>But soon the world cast shadows
On our joy</i>

34
00:04:56.875 --> 00:05:00.708
<i>In two short years
Our bed turned into a stadium</i>

35
00:05:00.792 --> 00:05:02.583
- When do we hear the good news?
- Exactly!

36
00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:03.684
You've done enough net practice.

37
00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:04.976
- Time to play the actual game.
- Exactly!

38
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.518
You've got your whole life ahead
of you to "build your careers."

39
00:05:06.542 --> 00:05:07.417
Exactly!

40
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.500
- Your biological clock's ticking!
- Exactly!

41
00:05:09.583 --> 00:05:11.792
- You want pure <i>shilajit?</i> You'll get it.
- Exactly!

42
00:05:11.875 --> 00:05:13.042
A cot beats a bed any day,

43
00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:16.958
- just stick a pillow under the waist!
- Exactly!

44
00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:21.000
It says two full pink lines.

45
00:05:21.083 --> 00:05:22.917
- Right?
- These are two full pink lines!

46
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.500
They're not dark enough to be sure.

47
00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.500
Please try once again.

48
00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.625
Why don't <i>you </i>try?
My bladder's empty.

49
00:06:30.458 --> 00:06:32.417
- He's lying.
- He's totally lying!

50
00:06:32.917 --> 00:06:33.917
This is from last night.

51
00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:35.458
- Where'd you meet her?
- Online.

52
00:06:36.042 --> 00:06:37.333
Does your wife know?

53
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.875
He thinks I don't know.

54
00:06:38.958 --> 00:06:41.167
Extra-tight T-shirts,
expensive deodorants,

55
00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.625
spending hours in the bathroom.

56
00:06:43.042 --> 00:06:44.562
- Shibhu, it's not funny.
- Yeah, I know.

57
00:06:45.542 --> 00:06:47.333
- Did you guys kiss?
- Just a peck.

58
00:06:48.625 --> 00:06:50.708
- No tongue.
- She's got an MBA.

59
00:06:50.792 --> 00:06:52.167
And I'm a mechanical engineer.

60
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.875
MA in Psychology.
I mean, what are we doing, girls?

61
00:06:55.292 --> 00:06:56.875
No tongue, no cheating.

62
00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:57.958
No cheating?

63
00:06:58.042 --> 00:06:58.917
Seriously.

64
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.833
Ma, I'm heading out with Anaya!

65
00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.667
Okay, but no going past the gate.

66
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.042
You've got such a perfect life, Kajol.

67
00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:07.667
Perfect? Nonsense!

68
00:07:07.708 --> 00:07:11.333
Perfect holidays, perfect food,
perfect relationships!

69
00:07:11.625 --> 00:07:13.458
I swear! It all looks perfect.

70
00:07:18.042 --> 00:07:19.542
They've got the wrong idea

71
00:07:19.917 --> 00:07:22.042
because of what I post on social media.

72
00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:26.500
<i>When life grows dim and loses spark</i>

73
00:07:30.458 --> 00:07:35.750
<i>My posts turn more colorful
To light the dark</i>

74
00:07:38.208 --> 00:07:40.167
<i>But real life…</i>

75
00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:42.042
Real life hides somewhere

76
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.000
behind those posts.

77
00:07:44.083 --> 00:07:46.184
Kajol, please try to understand,
I'm not arguing with you.

78
00:07:46.208 --> 00:07:47.500
I'm explaining!

79
00:07:47.583 --> 00:07:50.292
And I'm not listening to you.
I'm ignoring you!

80
00:07:50.375 --> 00:07:52.101
At least look at me
when I am talking to you!

81
00:07:52.125 --> 00:07:53.684
Humans have evolved,
for your information!

82
00:07:53.708 --> 00:07:55.268
We listen with our ears now, not our eyes!

83
00:07:55.292 --> 00:07:58.292
How many times do I have to tell you?
Don't leave your wet towel on the bed!

84
00:08:00.542 --> 00:08:05.167
Ever since I started having an affair,
my married life has actually improved.

85
00:08:05.333 --> 00:08:08.750
I mean, all that nagging
and irritation of married life?

86
00:08:08.833 --> 00:08:09.833
It's all gone now.

87
00:08:10.125 --> 00:08:13.333
I met Kajol 19 years ago.

88
00:08:14.875 --> 00:08:16.667
Before her, I'd met plenty of girls…

89
00:08:17.333 --> 00:08:19.458
But none of their hands
ever fit into mine.

90
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:21.809
Our fingers would always get tangled up.

91
00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:26.750
But when I first held Kajol's
beautiful hands,

92
00:08:27.333 --> 00:08:29.417
everything just clicked.

93
00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.458
Like a long-lost puzzle
falling into place.

94
00:08:33.042 --> 00:08:34.042
What happened next?

95
00:08:34.833 --> 00:08:37.976
One day, I finally worked up the courage
and took her out on a date to Mamta Momos,

96
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.208
and popped the question.

97
00:08:40.208 --> 00:08:41.417
Yes!

98
00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:48.042
Kajol, look.
They're tearing down Mamta Momos!

99
00:08:48.125 --> 00:08:50.542
- What? I can't hear you!
<i>- They're tearing down…</i>

100
00:08:50.625 --> 00:08:51.625
What?

101
00:08:52.125 --> 00:08:53.500
What about Mamta Momos?

102
00:08:54.208 --> 00:08:56.875
They're tearing down Mamta Momos,
the monument of our love!

103
00:08:56.958 --> 00:08:58.292
<i>Can you see this?</i>

104
00:08:58.375 --> 00:08:59.375
Oh, shit!

105
00:08:59.458 --> 00:09:01.958
Damn it!
Does this look like the time to talk?!

106
00:09:03.458 --> 00:09:04.500
Just record it!

107
00:09:04.583 --> 00:09:08.333
<i>When you get used to each other</i>

108
00:09:08.417 --> 00:09:11.833
<i>Every special thing becomes ordinary</i>

109
00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:14.750
<i>Electric bill and kids' vaccine</i>

110
00:09:15.417 --> 00:09:19.167
<i>Flat's EMI, a broken washing machine</i>

111
00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:23.917
<i>We've found so many ways
To stay busy every day</i>

112
00:09:24.417 --> 00:09:31.167
<i>That we meet each other
Like strangers every day</i>

113
00:09:32.042 --> 00:09:34.000
<i>Even while lying
next to each other in bed,</i>

114
00:09:34.083 --> 00:09:35.875
<i>our eyes stay fixed on our screens.</i>

115
00:09:36.792 --> 00:09:39.542
<i>We're scared that if we
actually look at each other,</i>

116
00:09:39.917 --> 00:09:43.292
<i>maybe there won't be anything left to say.</i>

117
00:10:14.042 --> 00:10:15.125
We had a lot of fun.

118
00:10:35.625 --> 00:10:36.750
I'm forgetful.

119
00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.458
One time, we left the shopping mall…

120
00:10:39.542 --> 00:10:41.750
A family photo at the Taj Mahal

121
00:10:42.458 --> 00:10:44.333
hangs on the living room wall.

122
00:10:45.417 --> 00:10:48.875
Even if it were lost, no one would notice.

123
00:10:49.208 --> 00:10:53.333
<i>Just a square mark would be left behind</i>

124
00:10:53.917 --> 00:10:56.958
<i>No one would miss it, trust me</i>

125
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:03.292
<i>That's my status in the house, too
You see</i>

126
00:11:03.875 --> 00:11:05.500
<i>I'm like that photo</i>

127
00:11:07.375 --> 00:11:10.333
Before marriage,
I had a few dreams of my own.

128
00:11:11.417 --> 00:11:14.792
<i>But I set all my dreams aside</i>

129
00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:19.500
<i>To dedicate myself to everyone else's</i>

130
00:11:20.292 --> 00:11:23.542
<i>Everyone's dreams
Took their flight eventually</i>

131
00:11:23.625 --> 00:11:28.833
<i>And now, they don't have
Any time for little old me</i>

132
00:11:28.917 --> 00:11:33.583
My only regret is that
I kept my dreams at bay for so long…

133
00:11:34.458 --> 00:11:36.667
That even they grew cold and turned away.

134
00:11:36.958 --> 00:11:41.083
<i>Now, there's only one question in my heart</i>

135
00:11:41.333 --> 00:11:45.458
<i>Who am I living for?</i>

136
00:11:45.792 --> 00:11:49.917
<i>How do I spend the rest of my life?</i>

137
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:55.208
<i>For I've always been the caretaker</i>

138
00:11:55.708 --> 00:12:00.750
<i>But I never learned to take care of myself</i>

139
00:12:04.208 --> 00:12:06.168
We don't get a holiday
for Holi here in Bangalore.

140
00:12:06.792 --> 00:12:09.917
It's just us covered in colors.

141
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.417
You should've come.

142
00:12:11.875 --> 00:12:14.167
It was so much fun!

143
00:12:14.417 --> 00:12:15.542
So much fun!

144
00:12:15.708 --> 00:12:17.389
<i>By the way,
my flight's delayed by an hour.</i>

145
00:12:17.458 --> 00:12:18.625
- Is he the same guy?
- Okay.

146
00:12:18.875 --> 00:12:19.875
Anand, right?

147
00:12:19.958 --> 00:12:21.208
<i>- No, it's…</i>
- Oh!

148
00:12:21.292 --> 00:12:22.500
The one from Delhi?

149
00:12:22.792 --> 00:12:24.333
- See you at home.
<i>- Okay. Bye.</i>

150
00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.583
Home? Finally, some action?

151
00:12:26.667 --> 00:12:28.708
Hey! We're serious, okay?

152
00:12:29.208 --> 00:12:30.792
- Very serious.
- Serious!

153
00:12:30.875 --> 00:12:32.125
He's the one!

154
00:12:32.375 --> 00:12:33.667
- Not possible.
- Are you sure?

155
00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.167
He's the one, I'm sure.

156
00:12:35.458 --> 00:12:38.292
- One hundred percent! Sure!
- Hundred percent!

157
00:12:38.375 --> 00:12:39.583
Oh, my God!

158
00:12:39.667 --> 00:12:42.208
Hundred percent… sure.

159
00:12:42.375 --> 00:12:44.167
Okay, Chumki.

160
00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.375
Actually, I'm not sure.

161
00:12:48.042 --> 00:12:49.083
I'm never sure.

162
00:12:49.625 --> 00:12:52.625
I'm permanently confused.
My status is unsure.

163
00:12:53.667 --> 00:12:55.250
This is my first problem…

164
00:12:55.917 --> 00:12:57.167
And it's got no cure.

165
00:12:57.833 --> 00:13:00.792
I was the class topper
and my family's biggest hope.

166
00:13:01.375 --> 00:13:03.875
<i>Everyone expected me to become a doctor.</i>

167
00:13:04.417 --> 00:13:07.833
<i>But then I realized it wasn't
the human body that intrigued me,</i>

168
00:13:07.958 --> 00:13:09.500
<i>but the mysteries of the mind.</i>

169
00:13:09.792 --> 00:13:11.875
<i>So, I switched to psychology.</i>

170
00:13:12.375 --> 00:13:14.417
<i>But that too was not my cup of tea.</i>

171
00:13:14.875 --> 00:13:17.375
<i>Finally, I dropped everything
and did my MBA.</i>

172
00:13:18.042 --> 00:13:20.708
<i>Standing in line, CV in hand.
It's a rat race.</i>

173
00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:22.292
It's a crazy maze.

174
00:13:22.375 --> 00:13:25.167
In fact,
the only thing I'm sure of is that

175
00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.583
I'm confused.

176
00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:28.500
Always confused.

177
00:13:28.583 --> 00:13:31.458
My second problem?
I just can't confront anyone.

178
00:13:31.583 --> 00:13:33.059
Bullying in school, ragging in college.

179
00:13:33.083 --> 00:13:34.458
<i>Now my boss harasses me every day.</i>

180
00:13:34.542 --> 00:13:36.667
It's… disgusting!

181
00:13:36.958 --> 00:13:39.958
I feel like giving him a whack!
But what can I do?

182
00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.875
I'm a coward like that.

183
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.542
Third problem?
I'm a little awkward socially.

184
00:13:44.792 --> 00:13:50.125
<i>I have a thousand emotions
And no clue how to express them</i>

185
00:13:50.625 --> 00:13:56.042
<i>There's always a raging battle between
Thoughts in my head and the words I say</i>

186
00:13:56.542 --> 00:14:00.042
<i>Thank God for emojis!</i>

187
00:14:01.583 --> 00:14:04.750
So I can have a conversation without
having to say anything.

188
00:14:05.125 --> 00:14:07.208
<i>I need two drinks to start talking,</i>

189
00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.458
<i>but after four drinks,
I can't stop throwing up.</i>

190
00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:13.458
So my situation is such that…

191
00:14:48.542 --> 00:14:49.542
What a guy!

192
00:14:49.792 --> 00:14:51.512
We thought he came down
to Bangalore for us.

193
00:14:51.583 --> 00:14:53.542
Did you know he has a girl here
in Bangalore?

194
00:14:53.667 --> 00:14:55.125
- Not interested.
- What's her name?

195
00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.309
Why even bother to find out?

196
00:14:56.333 --> 00:14:57.893
He switches girlfriends
every three months.

197
00:14:57.917 --> 00:14:58.792
Nonsense.

198
00:14:58.875 --> 00:15:00.315
We're already into the fourth month.

199
00:15:00.875 --> 00:15:02.583
- She's very special, okay?
- Yeah.

200
00:15:02.792 --> 00:15:04.912
So what's this "special" girl's name?
What's her name?

201
00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.417
- Of course, I know.
- Have some shame.

202
00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:07.660
I know her name. Are you mad?

203
00:15:07.708 --> 00:15:09.583
- Have some shame.
- Wait… Are you crazy?

204
00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:10.708
One second…

205
00:15:11.208 --> 00:15:13.292
- It's something sweet…
- Fruity!

206
00:15:13.625 --> 00:15:14.500
Sweetie!

207
00:15:14.583 --> 00:15:15.458
- Oh!
- See!

208
00:15:15.542 --> 00:15:16.417
- Sweetie!
- Sweetie!

209
00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.958
Sweetie's the love
of my life right now, guys.

210
00:15:19.125 --> 00:15:20.000
Hotel?

211
00:15:20.083 --> 00:15:21.917
No, I've got arrangements in every city.

212
00:15:22.667 --> 00:15:23.958
Hey, listen, stop on the left.

213
00:15:24.042 --> 00:15:25.125
Stop on the left, yeah.

214
00:15:27.292 --> 00:15:28.792
Look at that guy!

215
00:15:29.167 --> 00:15:31.542
- Okay, see you guys!
- Okay!

216
00:15:32.042 --> 00:15:33.042
Bye!

217
00:15:33.417 --> 00:15:34.292
- Bye!
- Bye!

218
00:15:34.417 --> 00:15:36.458
- Full-style, bro?
- Happy Holi, bro!

219
00:15:36.583 --> 00:15:38.042
- Happy Holi, bro! Check!
- Catch this.

220
00:15:38.333 --> 00:15:40.726
Tell me the address, quick! We've
been going around in circles forever.

221
00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:41.750
Undress?

222
00:15:42.958 --> 00:15:45.667
No, address! Not "undress", address!

223
00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.191
- Just tell us already.
- Note it down.

224
00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:48.750
- 301…
- Speak up.

225
00:15:48.917 --> 00:15:50.042
301…

226
00:15:50.125 --> 00:15:51.375
Bhakti Niwas.

227
00:15:51.583 --> 00:15:52.833
Bhakti Aaa...

228
00:15:53.042 --> 00:15:54.417
301, Bhakti Niwas.

229
00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.542
Sixth Cross.

230
00:15:55.708 --> 00:15:59.125
- Miller's Road.
- Miller's Road.

231
00:15:59.917 --> 00:16:00.917
- But…
- Bye!

232
00:16:02.542 --> 00:16:03.417
The keys?

233
00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.000
- I'm fine.
- Look in her bag.

234
00:16:05.083 --> 00:16:06.500
Under the mat?

235
00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:11.375
- Where are the keys?
- I found the keys!

236
00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.500
Listen.

237
00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.583
- She's so cute.
- We can't drive.

238
00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.292
We can't drive, so call a cab.

239
00:16:20.667 --> 00:16:21.667
Yeah, baby?

240
00:16:22.125 --> 00:16:23.125
How long?

241
00:16:25.333 --> 00:16:26.893
Yeah, the house is empty.
No one's here.

242
00:16:27.542 --> 00:16:28.862
Don't wear anything with buttons.

243
00:16:29.625 --> 00:16:30.875
Okay, baby, bye.

244
00:16:31.208 --> 00:16:33.042
Hurry up, okay?
I'm in the mood.

245
00:16:33.958 --> 00:16:34.958
Bye.

246
00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:42.250
Hello?

247
00:16:42.625 --> 00:16:44.000
<i>Hello, who's this?</i>

248
00:16:45.042 --> 00:16:46.125
You called, so you tell me.

249
00:16:46.292 --> 00:16:47.292
<i>Where's Chumki?</i>

250
00:16:47.542 --> 00:16:48.542
<i>Give her the phone.</i>

251
00:16:49.417 --> 00:16:51.583
Bro, I'm not her servant.

252
00:16:51.792 --> 00:16:52.667
<i>Who the hell are you?</i>

253
00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:54.708
<i>Listen, I want to speak to my girlfriend.</i>

254
00:16:55.208 --> 00:16:57.083
She's not interested, bro.

255
00:16:57.208 --> 00:16:59.583
Let her be. Let her live her life.

256
00:16:59.667 --> 00:17:00.583
<i>This is not funny.</i>

257
00:17:00.667 --> 00:17:02.500
<i>Why do you even have her phone?
Chumki!</i>

258
00:17:02.583 --> 00:17:04.792
"No one can claim another's soul.

259
00:17:05.375 --> 00:17:07.750
True love needs trust to make it whole."

260
00:17:08.083 --> 00:17:09.083
Bye.

261
00:17:38.667 --> 00:17:39.667
Hello!

262
00:17:40.708 --> 00:17:41.708
Hello!

263
00:17:42.125 --> 00:17:43.167
Hello, wake up!

264
00:17:43.458 --> 00:17:45.833
Wake up already!

265
00:17:49.542 --> 00:17:50.958
Baby…

266
00:17:54.542 --> 00:17:55.917
Meow.

267
00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.250
Hello!

268
00:18:07.792 --> 00:18:08.792
Who are you?

269
00:18:22.667 --> 00:18:24.333
Thief!

270
00:18:24.458 --> 00:18:25.625
Please!

271
00:18:25.917 --> 00:18:28.500
Thief…

272
00:18:31.708 --> 00:18:34.292
Help!

273
00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.333
Thief! Thief!

274
00:18:36.958 --> 00:18:38.083
Help…

275
00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.708
- Thief!
- Stop!

276
00:18:46.208 --> 00:18:47.417
Is this your home?

277
00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.000
Is this your place?

278
00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.125
Seriously, look around.

279
00:18:52.958 --> 00:18:54.079
- Is this your place?
- Is it...

280
00:19:08.208 --> 00:19:09.583
Where's my house?

281
00:19:14.292 --> 00:19:16.000
Where's my house?

282
00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:21.208
Your body language kind of gave away
what you were talking about.

283
00:19:21.333 --> 00:19:23.917
He hinted that he's involved
in infertility.

284
00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.500
Infertility?

285
00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.125
You mean infidelity.

286
00:19:27.208 --> 00:19:28.625
Yeah, infidelity.

287
00:19:28.708 --> 00:19:31.083
It's nothing really.
He's just fooling around.

288
00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.042
- Fooling…
- Probably dealing with boredom, I guess.

289
00:19:34.958 --> 00:19:35.958
And you're justifying it?

290
00:19:36.083 --> 00:19:37.458
I'm not justifying it.

291
00:19:37.667 --> 00:19:39.458
Everyone has their own
sense of morality.

292
00:19:40.792 --> 00:19:42.268
I feel really bad for Priya, you know.

293
00:19:42.292 --> 00:19:43.792
Good night, Ma.
Good night, Papa.

294
00:19:43.875 --> 00:19:45.000
- Good night.
- Good night.

295
00:19:45.083 --> 00:19:46.625
- Love you.
- Love you too.

296
00:19:49.625 --> 00:19:52.958
So, do you keep things from me?

297
00:19:54.125 --> 00:19:57.000
I know you also want to fool around.

298
00:20:01.083 --> 00:20:02.833
Look, if you do it, I'll do it too.

299
00:20:02.958 --> 00:20:04.250
What?

300
00:20:04.333 --> 00:20:05.875
But I haven't done anything, right?

301
00:20:05.958 --> 00:20:08.184
You're totally off track here.
"If you do it, I'll do it too."

302
00:20:08.208 --> 00:20:09.250
I'm just saying.

303
00:20:09.667 --> 00:20:10.958
I'm so sorry.

304
00:20:11.042 --> 00:20:13.750
- Yeah, yeah, no problem.
- I thought this was my…

305
00:20:14.917 --> 00:20:16.000
- My bag.
- Oh, yes.

306
00:20:16.083 --> 00:20:17.083
Oh shit!

307
00:20:17.292 --> 00:20:18.708
Not now.

308
00:20:19.167 --> 00:20:21.143
Hurry up and leave,
my girlfriend will be here any second.

309
00:20:21.167 --> 00:20:22.042
Parth?

310
00:20:22.125 --> 00:20:24.184
Great, one girlfriend leaves,
and the other walks right in.

311
00:20:24.208 --> 00:20:26.125
- No, baby.
- Who's next after me?

312
00:20:26.208 --> 00:20:27.083
You cheat!

313
00:20:27.167 --> 00:20:28.647
- Excuse me, there's been a...
- Shut up!

314
00:20:28.833 --> 00:20:30.958
- Baby, she just got here by accident.
- Oh wow!

315
00:20:31.042 --> 00:20:32.667
Her clothes were taken off by mistake.

316
00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.375
You have shown your true nature.

317
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.333
- What?
- Unbelievable.

318
00:20:36.417 --> 00:20:37.542
Don't call me again.

319
00:20:47.292 --> 00:20:48.292
What's your address?

320
00:20:49.042 --> 00:20:50.583
301, Bhakti Awaas.

321
00:20:50.667 --> 00:20:51.667
What?

322
00:20:51.792 --> 00:20:53.000
301, Bhakti...

323
00:20:54.875 --> 00:20:55.875
Bhakti Niwas.

324
00:20:55.917 --> 00:20:56.917
Let's go.

325
00:21:16.292 --> 00:21:17.875
Bhakti Awaas.

326
00:21:18.542 --> 00:21:19.583
Be careful there.

327
00:21:19.875 --> 00:21:20.917
Watch your step.

328
00:21:21.458 --> 00:21:22.875
Helmet, my helmet.

329
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.000
What?!

330
00:21:42.292 --> 00:21:43.708
I can't believe this.

331
00:21:44.125 --> 00:21:45.667
<i>Sis, this isn't funny, okay?</i>

332
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.000
It's not funny.

333
00:21:47.083 --> 00:21:47.958
<i>Kajol, you shut up.</i>

334
00:21:48.042 --> 00:21:49.500
<i>- This is serious.</i>
- Oh God!

335
00:21:49.583 --> 00:21:51.184
His mom's already called like three times

336
00:21:51.208 --> 00:21:53.625
and said they'll delay
the engagement.

337
00:21:54.708 --> 00:21:56.208
Should I call her, Ma?

338
00:21:56.292 --> 00:21:57.292
Absolutely not.

339
00:21:57.333 --> 00:21:58.750
No need for any explanations.

340
00:21:58.833 --> 00:22:00.250
He should trust you.

341
00:22:00.583 --> 00:22:02.833
Who would trust this story?

342
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:05.833
Who'd believe the confusion between
Bhakti Awaas and Bhakti Niwas?

343
00:22:05.917 --> 00:22:08.042
Chumki, you're the only one
who could pull this off.

344
00:22:08.125 --> 00:22:09.750
- This isn't funny!
- I have an idea.

345
00:22:09.958 --> 00:22:11.833
Take Anand to Bhakti Awaas.

346
00:22:12.083 --> 00:22:14.042
- It's Bhakti Niwas, Ma.
- Whatever.

347
00:22:14.125 --> 00:22:16.292
Take him there,
he'll see it with his own eyes

348
00:22:16.375 --> 00:22:17.583
and believe you.

349
00:22:17.667 --> 00:22:19.000
Chumki, you're not doing that.

350
00:22:19.083 --> 00:22:20.750
Anand should trust you.

351
00:22:20.833 --> 00:22:22.674
You two are going
to spend your lives together!

352
00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:24.542
Don't mislead her, Kajol.

353
00:22:24.625 --> 00:22:26.625
Ma, I agree, we need to do something.

354
00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:28.958
Take him there.
He'll see it himself.

355
00:22:29.042 --> 00:22:30.458
It wouldn't be an issue

356
00:22:30.542 --> 00:22:33.167
- if he were that easy to convince.
- What a jerk he is, you know!

357
00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:34.167
Just stop it.

358
00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:35.958
Fine, hold on.
Should I talk to him?

359
00:22:36.875 --> 00:22:38.333
Guys, please, stop it.

360
00:22:38.417 --> 00:22:39.875
Don't give him that much importance.

361
00:22:40.042 --> 00:22:42.667
I'll talk to him, explain it nicely,
and he'll understand.

362
00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:44.831
Chumki, don't listen to her.
Listen, I'm telling you.

363
00:22:44.875 --> 00:22:46.833
No, I think I should talk to him.

364
00:22:46.917 --> 00:22:47.792
I'll sort it out.

365
00:22:47.875 --> 00:22:48.893
No, Chumki, just listen to me.

366
00:22:48.917 --> 00:22:50.250
One sec, you listen to me first.

367
00:22:50.417 --> 00:22:51.726
- Kajol, stay out of this.
- I'll handle it.

368
00:22:51.750 --> 00:22:53.684
You don't need to do it.
That's what I'm trying to say!

369
00:22:53.708 --> 00:22:55.042
Can I say something, guys?

370
00:22:55.208 --> 00:22:56.833
Let her decide.

371
00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:58.768
- She'll decide, Ma. I'm just telling her.
- Let me decide.

372
00:22:58.792 --> 00:23:00.952
- You just have to…
- I can't handle two mothers at once.

373
00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.143
- She interferes with everything.
- Fine, bye-bye.

374
00:23:02.167 --> 00:23:03.042
I'll handle it.

375
00:23:03.125 --> 00:23:04.125
- Bye.
- Bye.

376
00:23:30.458 --> 00:23:31.708
- Hey, you!
- Watch out.

377
00:23:34.417 --> 00:23:35.917
- What?
- You're trying to run me over?

378
00:23:36.167 --> 00:23:38.458
You go back inside.

379
00:23:38.667 --> 00:23:39.667
Baba!

380
00:23:39.792 --> 00:23:40.917
Can't you see the signal?

381
00:23:41.125 --> 00:23:42.667
Just keep quiet and come inside!

382
00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:44.309
- Look at me, you were trying to...
- Baba, come inside.

383
00:23:44.333 --> 00:23:45.208
- No, I wasn't!
- Come on.

384
00:23:45.292 --> 00:23:46.917
- Baba!
- I'm coming!

385
00:23:47.042 --> 00:23:48.542
Are you coming,
or should I come down?

386
00:23:48.667 --> 00:23:49.792
- Go on.
- Baba.

387
00:23:49.875 --> 00:23:51.083
- Coming!
- Baba!

388
00:23:52.417 --> 00:23:53.917
- Alright, go.
- Just come inside!

389
00:23:54.542 --> 00:23:57.167
Why do you do that?
Scold me in front of everyone?

390
00:23:57.250 --> 00:23:58.792
Why do you keep
doing stuff like that?

391
00:23:58.875 --> 00:24:00.676
If you don't do it,
I won't have to scold you.

392
00:24:00.958 --> 00:24:02.083
Here are your meds.

393
00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.125
Don't forget to take them.

394
00:24:05.167 --> 00:24:06.167
Anything else?

395
00:24:06.542 --> 00:24:08.417
Just turn off the washing machine.

396
00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:09.958
You don't need to dry the clothes.

397
00:24:10.042 --> 00:24:12.500
And you've got some invites.

398
00:24:12.625 --> 00:24:14.875
Go through them when you can.
I'll be late today.

399
00:24:15.292 --> 00:24:16.500
Oh, you forgot your charger.

400
00:24:17.208 --> 00:24:19.583
I forget everything because of you.

401
00:24:19.667 --> 00:24:20.792
So this is my fault too?

402
00:24:21.708 --> 00:24:22.708
Yes, of course.

403
00:24:22.833 --> 00:24:23.833
Who else do I have?

404
00:24:37.792 --> 00:24:39.458
<i>Announces the departure of its flight…</i>

405
00:24:39.542 --> 00:24:42.542
Hello? Who's this?

406
00:24:42.708 --> 00:24:44.809
<i>All passengers are requested
to please proceed towards the gate…</i>

407
00:24:44.833 --> 00:24:45.833
Who?

408
00:24:47.667 --> 00:24:49.292
Okay. So, who are you?

409
00:24:50.208 --> 00:24:51.500
Your wife's friend.

410
00:24:52.083 --> 00:24:53.083
And I am?

411
00:24:54.167 --> 00:24:55.500
My friend's husband.

412
00:24:55.708 --> 00:24:57.250
The one who dropped me off at home.

413
00:24:57.542 --> 00:24:58.542
On his bike?

414
00:24:59.958 --> 00:25:01.518
The one who spoke
to him over the phone?

415
00:25:01.542 --> 00:25:03.333
- Who?
- Anand!

416
00:25:04.083 --> 00:25:05.417
- Okay, so I'm both.
- Yes.

417
00:25:06.125 --> 00:25:07.125
Okay.

418
00:25:07.208 --> 00:25:08.542
Good. Nice.

419
00:25:09.667 --> 00:25:10.667
Okay, so what's the plan?

420
00:25:11.542 --> 00:25:13.375
Tonight, my colleagues are having a party.

421
00:25:13.458 --> 00:25:14.333
Alright.

422
00:25:14.417 --> 00:25:17.167
So you and your wife, aka my friend,

423
00:25:17.792 --> 00:25:19.125
will run into me and Anand.

424
00:25:19.208 --> 00:25:20.083
Okay?

425
00:25:20.167 --> 00:25:21.750
It'll clear up his doubts.

426
00:25:21.958 --> 00:25:23.143
He'll obviously see that we didn't…

427
00:25:23.167 --> 00:25:24.208
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

428
00:25:25.708 --> 00:25:27.829
If he's that suspicious,
why don't you just leave him?

429
00:25:27.958 --> 00:25:29.458
I didn't ask for relationship advice.

430
00:25:29.833 --> 00:25:31.042
If you can't help me, then…

431
00:25:31.125 --> 00:25:32.326
But who's going to be my wife?

432
00:25:33.333 --> 00:25:34.333
You have someone in mind?

433
00:25:34.667 --> 00:25:36.458
Single, under 25, and beautiful?

434
00:25:37.042 --> 00:25:38.042
Know anyone?

435
00:25:39.708 --> 00:25:40.833
Fine, I'll take care of it.

436
00:25:42.583 --> 00:25:45.375
In the meantime,
book me a flight and hotel.

437
00:25:45.583 --> 00:25:47.125
- Business Class, of course.
- Done.

438
00:25:47.667 --> 00:25:48.947
I only stay in five-star hotels.

439
00:25:50.750 --> 00:25:51.750
Hey, Shruti…

440
00:25:51.958 --> 00:25:53.417
So we are a couple.

441
00:25:53.500 --> 00:25:55.542
Chumki was with us.
We got sloshed.

442
00:25:55.625 --> 00:25:57.833
And my boss's name is Anand,
and you hate him.

443
00:25:57.917 --> 00:25:58.917
Yes, yes.

444
00:25:59.833 --> 00:26:02.167
I know all of Chumki's friends,

445
00:26:02.333 --> 00:26:04.458
but I haven't heard of you two before.

446
00:26:05.083 --> 00:26:06.125
Shruti.

447
00:26:06.542 --> 00:26:08.167
She's a colleague.
I told you about her.

448
00:26:08.250 --> 00:26:09.125
Yes.

449
00:26:09.208 --> 00:26:10.208
Shruti what?

450
00:26:10.292 --> 00:26:11.292
Shukla.

451
00:26:11.792 --> 00:26:12.667
And you?

452
00:26:12.750 --> 00:26:13.958
Parth Nakul Sahadev.

453
00:26:15.750 --> 00:26:17.500
Wait, you're a Shukla
and he's a Sahadev?

454
00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:20.625
Confusing, right?

455
00:26:20.875 --> 00:26:22.143
Yesterday was even more confusing.

456
00:26:22.167 --> 00:26:23.476
- So we got…
- Don't drink, don't drink.

457
00:26:23.500 --> 00:26:25.518
- You really shouldn't be drinking anymore.
- I'm fine.

458
00:26:25.542 --> 00:26:27.375
- You're not fine.
- Yeah, exactly.

459
00:26:27.458 --> 00:26:28.851
The same thing happened
yesterday, too, right?

460
00:26:28.875 --> 00:26:30.167
It's so embarrassing.

461
00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:31.917
You didn't tell us what you do.

462
00:26:32.917 --> 00:26:35.417
Well, my target is
to win the Green Nobel 2025.

463
00:26:36.375 --> 00:26:38.667
I'm working on the automated
absorption and assimilation

464
00:26:38.750 --> 00:26:42.625
of the cosmic vitality for
the self-irrigation and sustainability

465
00:26:42.708 --> 00:26:43.792
of the human condition.

466
00:26:44.875 --> 00:26:47.750
Basically, I invented
human photosynthesis.

467
00:26:49.208 --> 00:26:50.208
What?

468
00:26:50.625 --> 00:26:51.625
Trees…

469
00:26:53.208 --> 00:26:54.958
Ever seen trees working?

470
00:26:57.458 --> 00:26:58.708
Getting scolded by their boss?

471
00:26:59.292 --> 00:27:00.417
- No.
- Why?

472
00:27:00.750 --> 00:27:02.417
Because trees make their own food.

473
00:27:04.458 --> 00:27:06.125
So, what's the basic need for humans?

474
00:27:06.542 --> 00:27:07.542
Food, right?

475
00:27:08.208 --> 00:27:09.667
So, we need to become like trees.

476
00:27:11.500 --> 00:27:12.833
- How?
- Very simple process.

477
00:27:12.917 --> 00:27:15.500
Wake up early, face the sun,

478
00:27:15.625 --> 00:27:17.042
and raise one hand.

479
00:27:17.208 --> 00:27:18.833
It acts like an antenna.

480
00:27:18.917 --> 00:27:21.958
Put the other hand down here.

481
00:27:22.042 --> 00:27:24.375
Look down, aim, and pee on your feet.

482
00:27:25.417 --> 00:27:28.417
You've got to nourish yourself
with your own water.

483
00:27:29.125 --> 00:27:31.042
That's it. Human photosynthesis.

484
00:27:31.750 --> 00:27:33.000
Produce your own food.

485
00:27:33.208 --> 00:27:34.083
That's the idea.

486
00:27:34.167 --> 00:27:35.625
He's joking.

487
00:27:35.875 --> 00:27:37.458
He's actually a travel blogger.

488
00:27:37.583 --> 00:27:38.875
He has 150,000 followers.

489
00:27:39.042 --> 00:27:40.500
He's got a weird sense of humor,

490
00:27:40.750 --> 00:27:42.208
but he's a good soul.

491
00:27:42.583 --> 00:27:43.667
He's got a big heart.

492
00:27:44.292 --> 00:27:46.332
Yeah, I can't show you
what is bigger than my heart.

493
00:27:46.458 --> 00:27:47.458
Come on, Parth.

494
00:27:50.208 --> 00:27:51.292
It's a joke.

495
00:27:51.500 --> 00:27:53.417
Brain, guys.
You guys have dirty minds.

496
00:27:55.833 --> 00:27:58.250
This is actually a tradition
in our group.

497
00:27:58.375 --> 00:28:00.417
We all share our love stories musically.

498
00:28:00.542 --> 00:28:01.833
Just wait. You'll have fun!

499
00:28:01.917 --> 00:28:05.042
So, listen, here's what happened…

500
00:28:05.667 --> 00:28:06.958
We're a couple, you know.

501
00:28:07.250 --> 00:28:09.333
And Chumki was with us.

502
00:28:09.458 --> 00:28:11.792
My boss's name is also Anand.

503
00:28:12.333 --> 00:28:13.750
Parth really hates him.

504
00:28:14.042 --> 00:28:15.167
So, in his drunken stupor,

505
00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:17.333
he picked up your call
and screwed you over.

506
00:28:25.333 --> 00:28:28.292
<i>Both Tinder and Aisle
Matched our profile</i>

507
00:28:28.750 --> 00:28:31.750
<i>His bio was unique
And radius within a mile</i>

508
00:28:31.833 --> 00:28:35.958
<i>After 52 right swipes
This miracle transpired</i>

509
00:28:36.042 --> 00:28:38.292
I was totally worth it, okay?

510
00:28:38.625 --> 00:28:43.208
