756
00:42:55.667 --> 00:42:56.958
<i>Till things are alright</i>

757
00:43:03.333 --> 00:43:04.667
<i>Till things are alright</i>

758
00:43:15.458 --> 00:43:16.458
<i>Hi.</i>

759
00:43:16.625 --> 00:43:17.625
<i>Hey.</i>

760
00:43:18.250 --> 00:43:19.625
<i>Single or married?</i>

761
00:43:20.542 --> 00:43:21.542
<i>You first.</i>

762
00:43:23.042 --> 00:43:24.792
<i>Married and bored.</i>

763
00:43:32.667 --> 00:43:35.500
<i>It's the story of every home
and household.</i>

764
00:43:35.583 --> 00:43:36.583
<i>Same here.</i>

765
00:43:39.125 --> 00:43:40.667
<i>Why? Your wife is boring?</i>

766
00:43:42.292 --> 00:43:43.917
Yes, yes. A little.

767
00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:45.375
<i>What about your husband?</i>

768
00:43:47.292 --> 00:43:49.333
<i>He's right now in the same room.</i>

769
00:43:52.250 --> 00:43:53.250
<i>Oh, poor thing.</i>

770
00:43:55.667 --> 00:43:58.292
<i>Don't sympathize,
he's a cheating rascal.</i>

771
00:43:59.333 --> 00:44:01.333
<i>Oh, sorry.</i>

772
00:44:05.208 --> 00:44:07.917
<i>WBU? This is your first affair?</i>

773
00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:16.417
Hey, what does "WBU"
mean in a text message?

774
00:44:17.958 --> 00:44:18.875
What about you?!

775
00:44:18.958 --> 00:44:20.542
Okay.

776
00:44:21.333 --> 00:44:23.833
<i>Are we having an affair?</i>

777
00:44:24.167 --> 00:44:26.708
<i>No,
I'm just here looking for siblings.</i>

778
00:44:32.250 --> 00:44:33.792
<i>You are quite funny.</i>

779
00:44:34.417 --> 00:44:36.292
<i>Not boring, right? Like your wife?</i>

780
00:44:39.917 --> 00:44:42.250
<i>You aren't like her at all.</i>

781
00:44:50.458 --> 00:44:53.292
<i>What do you look like right now?</i>

782
00:45:30.542 --> 00:45:33.542
OUR ROMEO AND JULIET
LOVE YOU BOTH

783
00:45:38.167 --> 00:45:39.583
- Done?
- Yeah.

784
00:45:45.625 --> 00:45:46.750
Rohan!

785
00:45:47.500 --> 00:45:48.375
Hello, Uncle.

786
00:45:48.458 --> 00:45:49.458
When did you get back?

787
00:45:49.875 --> 00:45:51.167
Day before yesterday.

788
00:45:51.958 --> 00:45:54.208
And you're showing up now,
after two whole days?

789
00:45:54.458 --> 00:45:55.458
Well…

790
00:45:57.458 --> 00:45:59.458
Bantu, come back tomorrow. Go on.

791
00:45:59.708 --> 00:46:01.000
Okay, see you tomorrow.

792
00:46:05.583 --> 00:46:06.625
If Aabir were with us,

793
00:46:07.333 --> 00:46:08.973
you'd have come straight
from the airport.

794
00:46:09.667 --> 00:46:10.667
Well…

795
00:46:11.042 --> 00:46:12.375
I couldn't avoid this trip.

796
00:46:12.667 --> 00:46:15.250
There are a few things I need
to wrap up.

797
00:46:16.500 --> 00:46:17.700
You're staying for a few days?

798
00:46:18.500 --> 00:46:20.292
Yeah, about eight to ten days.

799
00:46:20.875 --> 00:46:21.750
Once I leave this time,

800
00:46:21.833 --> 00:46:23.674
I probably won't be back for
a couple of years.

801
00:46:26.542 --> 00:46:27.625
Baba, I'm heading out.

802
00:46:27.917 --> 00:46:29.208
Weren't you going somewhere too?

803
00:46:29.292 --> 00:46:30.625
Rohan will drop you.

804
00:46:30.792 --> 00:46:32.417
No, Baba, I've already booked a cab.

805
00:46:36.875 --> 00:46:38.875
- Uncle, I should get going too.
- Alright, go ahead.

806
00:46:38.917 --> 00:46:40.476
- I'll come see you before I leave.
- Okay.

807
00:46:40.500 --> 00:46:41.500
Take care.

808
00:46:47.000 --> 00:46:49.833
Jhinuk! Jhinuk!
What do you want?

809
00:46:51.625 --> 00:46:53.826
You could've just called
and said you changed your mind.

810
00:46:53.875 --> 00:46:55.208
I rushed all the way from London…

811
00:46:55.625 --> 00:46:56.792
Just to head back alone?

812
00:46:57.042 --> 00:46:58.417
Rohan, please don't push me.

813
00:46:58.500 --> 00:46:59.833
We can't be together.

814
00:47:00.375 --> 00:47:01.375
Why not?

815
00:47:01.500 --> 00:47:02.500
Jhinuk!

816
00:47:14.583 --> 00:47:15.833
My friend likes you.

817
00:47:17.292 --> 00:47:18.292
Friend?

818
00:47:18.917 --> 00:47:19.917
Which friend?

819
00:47:27.292 --> 00:47:28.292
Just reply to her.

820
00:47:28.667 --> 00:47:29.667
She's waiting.

821
00:47:35.458 --> 00:47:36.500
You'll get me in trouble.

822
00:47:44.083 --> 00:47:45.250
Hello? Sir, hi.

823
00:47:45.625 --> 00:47:48.208
<i>Hey, Bombay Boy. What's going on?
Did you become a composer?</i>

824
00:47:48.375 --> 00:47:51.667
Nothing, just making music for ads.

825
00:47:51.917 --> 00:47:52.917
<i>What?</i>

826
00:47:53.583 --> 00:47:54.750
Just to survive.

827
00:47:55.625 --> 00:47:56.917
I get some money out of it.

828
00:47:57.417 --> 00:47:59.097
<i>If you're having money problems,
come back.</i>

829
00:47:59.750 --> 00:48:01.792
<i>We have a senior developer job open.</i>

830
00:48:02.292 --> 00:48:04.732
<i>Just thought I should ask our guy before
the interviews start.</i>

831
00:48:05.208 --> 00:48:06.708
Oh, okay.

832
00:48:07.333 --> 00:48:08.708
<i>It comes with a 20% hike.</i>

833
00:48:09.250 --> 00:48:10.542
Thank you. Okay.

834
00:48:10.750 --> 00:48:11.831
<i>Think about it and call me.</i>

835
00:48:20.625 --> 00:48:22.125
I have no idea what he's up to.

836
00:48:22.667 --> 00:48:24.792
Look, it just keeps showing "typing."

837
00:48:25.167 --> 00:48:26.167
Just call him already.

838
00:48:26.250 --> 00:48:28.250
If he wanted to talk,
he would've called.

839
00:48:28.750 --> 00:48:30.000
Why the ego, Man?

840
00:48:30.458 --> 00:48:31.875
It's not ego.

841
00:48:33.083 --> 00:48:36.833
Some things are just hard
to say on a call.

842
00:48:37.208 --> 00:48:38.792
It's easier over text.

843
00:48:39.083 --> 00:48:40.351
That's probably
why he's messaging.

844
00:48:40.375 --> 00:48:43.333
Shruti, stop forgetting your lunch!

845
00:48:44.042 --> 00:48:45.125
Oh! Thank you so much.

846
00:48:45.208 --> 00:48:46.309
I will pick you up at 8:00 a.m.

847
00:48:46.333 --> 00:48:47.250
Hello? Hey, bro.

848
00:48:47.333 --> 00:48:48.708
Listen, Parth.

849
00:48:48.958 --> 00:48:50.292
Bro, enough with the suspense.

850
00:48:50.375 --> 00:48:51.625
You've been typing forever.

851
00:48:51.750 --> 00:48:54.833
- Wait, are you with Shruti?
- I'm always so forgetful

852
00:48:54.917 --> 00:48:56.477
Yeah. Want me to hand the phone to her?

853
00:48:57.375 --> 00:49:00.083
No.
No, I'll talk to you later.

854
00:49:00.417 --> 00:49:03.125
- They're calling me inside.
- Okay.

855
00:49:03.208 --> 00:49:04.292
- Bye.
- Bye.

856
00:49:04.542 --> 00:49:05.542
Bye.

857
00:49:12.292 --> 00:49:13.792
Lunch exchange.

858
00:49:15.042 --> 00:49:16.208
So, he's the single father?

859
00:49:17.667 --> 00:49:18.667
Yeah.

860
00:49:19.792 --> 00:49:20.875
What?

861
00:49:21.208 --> 00:49:22.208
Nothing.

862
00:49:23.625 --> 00:49:24.708
Say something.

863
00:49:24.917 --> 00:49:26.101
See, my logic is pretty simple.

864
00:49:26.125 --> 00:49:27.667
Everyone deserves to be happy.

865
00:49:27.875 --> 00:49:29.434
Do whatever it takes
to make that happen.

866
00:49:29.458 --> 00:49:30.979
Just don't hurt anyone in the process.

867
00:49:36.917 --> 00:49:38.667
I think I really like this guy.

868
00:49:42.292 --> 00:49:44.208
He's got a ton of responsibilities,

869
00:49:44.292 --> 00:49:47.583
but he's still so sorted,
not boring at all, and he's really…

870
00:49:48.250 --> 00:49:49.250
Parth!

871
00:49:50.083 --> 00:49:51.083
Parth!

872
00:49:54.792 --> 00:49:55.792
Sorry.

873
00:50:17.000 --> 00:50:18.667
Modern love is so confusing.

874
00:50:18.875 --> 00:50:22.417
It's like a cheese Chinese
Schezwan masala <i>dosa.</i>

875
00:50:22.792 --> 00:50:24.792
It's got stuff from Chennai
all the way to China,

876
00:50:24.875 --> 00:50:26.583
but doesn't really belong anywhere.

877
00:50:40.458 --> 00:50:42.208
Please don't laugh.

878
00:50:42.667 --> 00:50:44.587
Don't make me more embarrassed
than I already am.

879
00:50:46.417 --> 00:50:47.934
So, where are you originally from,
Delhi or Bangalore?

880
00:50:47.958 --> 00:50:49.208
Actually, Pune.

881
00:50:49.625 --> 00:50:51.208
But I work in Delhi.

882
00:50:51.458 --> 00:50:53.708
And my company's
headquarter is in Bangalore.

883
00:50:53.792 --> 00:50:55.434
- Oh, got it.
- So, I have to go there once a year.

884
00:50:55.458 --> 00:50:56.500
That's when…

885
00:50:58.458 --> 00:50:59.458
You?

886
00:50:59.750 --> 00:51:02.125
You do theater, right?

887
00:51:03.500 --> 00:51:04.500
Homework!

888
00:51:06.458 --> 00:51:08.417
I just do theater to pass the time.

889
00:51:08.625 --> 00:51:11.167
I'm actually currently working
on the stabilization

890
00:51:11.250 --> 00:51:13.458
of the follicular cells
for the epitherial…

891
00:51:13.708 --> 00:51:14.708
Okay, I get it.

892
00:51:14.792 --> 00:51:18.125
Basically, I'm trying to find a way
to permanently remove men's chest hair.

893
00:51:18.250 --> 00:51:20.000
You like a clean chest?
What is your thing?

894
00:51:20.167 --> 00:51:22.792
<i>The doors will open on your left.</i>

895
00:51:23.250 --> 00:51:24.250
I'm in HR.

896
00:51:24.625 --> 00:51:25.625
Human Remorse?

897
00:51:26.583 --> 00:51:27.583
Hit and Run?

898
00:51:27.750 --> 00:51:28.750
Hardly Relevant?

899
00:51:31.667 --> 00:51:32.667
Sorry.

900
00:51:34.958 --> 00:51:36.500
You and your beau work together?

901
00:51:37.167 --> 00:51:38.167
Yeah.

902
00:51:38.667 --> 00:51:40.458
Actually, I'm engaged.

903
00:51:40.667 --> 00:51:41.792
We're getting married soon.

904
00:51:41.917 --> 00:51:43.037
Why are you getting married?

905
00:51:45.000 --> 00:51:46.417
I like being with him.

906
00:51:46.792 --> 00:51:49.250
He's like my comfort zone.

907
00:51:51.500 --> 00:51:54.500
In behavioral psychology, that's
called the "house slippers syndrome".

908
00:51:54.792 --> 00:51:56.750
- What?
- You know house slippers?

909
00:51:57.250 --> 00:51:58.250
They're all worn out,

910
00:51:59.042 --> 00:52:00.083
but we still wear them.

911
00:52:00.917 --> 00:52:02.250
Because they're comfy.

912
00:52:02.333 --> 00:52:03.375
We're used to them.

913
00:52:04.583 --> 00:52:05.875
And we don't toss them out

914
00:52:06.417 --> 00:52:07.737
until they make us slip and fall.

915
00:52:11.750 --> 00:52:13.417
<i>So, why are you here?</i>

916
00:52:14.917 --> 00:52:15.792
<i>Sex...</i>

917
00:52:15.917 --> 00:52:19.417
<i>Explore the unexplored.
And you?</i>

918
00:52:21.917 --> 00:52:24.458
<i>To catch...
I'm looking for something.</i>

919
00:52:43.958 --> 00:52:46.750
You wrote that letter, right?

920
00:52:48.667 --> 00:52:49.667
I like you too.

921
00:52:57.042 --> 00:52:59.333
Look, what's this?
How'd it become black?

922
00:52:59.417 --> 00:53:00.667
It'll come out.

923
00:53:00.792 --> 00:53:03.875
So this is the lifeline.

924
00:53:09.708 --> 00:53:11.125
- Hi.
- Hi.

925
00:53:11.875 --> 00:53:13.417
- Are you busy?
- No, go ahead.

926
00:53:13.500 --> 00:53:14.958
I've been messaging you for a while.

927
00:53:16.042 --> 00:53:17.625
Sorry, I missed them.

928
00:53:18.000 --> 00:53:19.333
<i>Are you okay?
What is it?</i>

929
00:53:19.458 --> 00:53:20.458
Yeah…

930
00:53:21.083 --> 00:53:24.167
Well, Sameer called.

931
00:53:24.917 --> 00:53:26.958
<i>He's offering me a promotion
with a 20% hike.</i>

932
00:53:27.458 --> 00:53:28.875
He wants an answer by tonight.

933
00:53:30.542 --> 00:53:31.583
So what did you say?

934
00:53:33.125 --> 00:53:34.606
Nothing's really working out, Shruti.

935
00:53:37.208 --> 00:53:39.208
<i>I'm making jingles for damn iron rods.</i>

936
00:53:39.833 --> 00:53:40.875
<i>I'm just done.</i>

937
00:53:43.042 --> 00:53:46.625
Here, everything runs on contacts,
and I don't have any.

938
00:53:49.042 --> 00:53:50.042
What are you looking at?

939
00:53:51.583 --> 00:53:52.583
<i>No one.</i>

940
00:53:53.667 --> 00:53:54.707
<i>So, what have you decided?</i>

941
00:53:57.792 --> 00:53:59.083
I think I should take the job.

942
00:54:00.042 --> 00:54:01.042
<i>What do you think?</i>

943
00:54:02.250 --> 00:54:04.583
You've already made up your mind.
Why ask me?

944
00:54:05.333 --> 00:54:07.500
Shruti, I'm asking
because it should be our decision.

945
00:54:07.583 --> 00:54:11.042
No, it's your decision,
and it's the right one.

946
00:54:11.125 --> 00:54:12.125
It's practical.

947
00:54:14.375 --> 00:54:15.250
What about you?

948
00:54:15.333 --> 00:54:18.167
Me? I'll stay in Delhi.

949
00:54:18.917 --> 00:54:20.375
I'm getting a promotion too.

950
00:54:21.458 --> 00:54:23.375
<i>You did the right thing by quitting.</i>

951
00:54:23.792 --> 00:54:27.250
You were right
when you said you're average.

952
00:54:28.042 --> 00:54:29.083
<i>Like your father.</i>

953
00:54:30.292 --> 00:54:31.708
<i>You know what your problem is?</i>

954
00:54:31.958 --> 00:54:34.958
<i>You don't know
what you want from life.</i>

955
00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:37.042
<i>I'll talk to you later.</i>

956
00:54:37.125 --> 00:54:38.167
<i>I have to go.</i>

957
00:54:48.250 --> 00:54:50.125
<i>Is Maya your real name?</i>

958
00:54:51.833 --> 00:54:55.500
<i>Nope. What about you?
Are you actually a wing commander?</i>

959
00:54:56.250 --> 00:54:57.250
<i>No.</i>

960
00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:02.500
<i>At least with fake names,
we can be real here.</i>

961
00:55:02.583 --> 00:55:07.583
<i>True. I can tell you things I'd never say
to my husband.</i>

962
00:55:19.000 --> 00:55:20.375
Hello, my sweetheart!

963
00:55:20.583 --> 00:55:21.958
Hey, Auntie, are you free?

964
00:55:22.125 --> 00:55:23.500
For you, I'm always free.

965
00:55:23.792 --> 00:55:26.792
You know, my friend Anaya…

966
00:55:27.042 --> 00:55:29.167
<i>She's pretty confused.</i>

967
00:55:29.542 --> 00:55:32.917
She can't figure out
if she's straight or not.

968
00:55:33.292 --> 00:55:37.917
It's a confusion caused by the internet.

969
00:55:38.833 --> 00:55:42.208
At the young age of 15,
you guys have already seen

970
00:55:42.625 --> 00:55:44.265
things we might not have even seen by 25.

971
00:55:44.292 --> 00:55:46.417
Please just tell me, she's really upset.

972
00:55:46.542 --> 00:55:48.042
<i>Tell her not to worry.</i>

973
00:55:48.958 --> 00:55:51.667
One figures it out when the time is right.

974
00:55:52.792 --> 00:55:53.792
But…

975
00:55:54.458 --> 00:55:57.958
How will she know?
I mean, how will she officially know?

976
00:55:58.833 --> 00:55:59.833
It's very simple.

977
00:56:00.500 --> 00:56:02.375
One day, she'll kiss a girl,

978
00:56:02.875 --> 00:56:05.167
and if she feels
butterflies in her stomach,

979
00:56:05.500 --> 00:56:07.125
<i>then she likes girls.</i>

980
00:56:07.917 --> 00:56:09.917
<i>And if, while kissing a boy,</i>

981
00:56:10.083 --> 00:56:12.417
<i>she feels like she's floating,</i>

982
00:56:12.750 --> 00:56:13.875
<i>then she's straight.</i>

983
00:56:14.208 --> 00:56:15.083
Or maybe both.

984
00:56:15.167 --> 00:56:17.708
But your "friend" will figure it out.

985
00:56:18.417 --> 00:56:20.542
But, Auntie, this is…

986
00:56:21.583 --> 00:56:22.583
What about science?

987
00:56:22.833 --> 00:56:24.083
Baby, kiss test.

988
00:56:24.750 --> 00:56:26.070
<i>It's the oldest science there is.</i>

989
00:56:26.625 --> 00:56:29.333
Pihu, you'll know when the time is right.

990
00:56:29.417 --> 00:56:31.208
<i>Okay? Just chill out.</i>

991
00:56:31.375 --> 00:56:32.375
Okay, bye.

992
00:56:33.125 --> 00:56:34.125
Bye.

993
00:56:39.333 --> 00:56:40.375
Jhinuk!

994
00:56:44.958 --> 00:56:46.792
This is your interview letter.

995
00:56:48.500 --> 00:56:50.417
My university wants to interview you.

996
00:56:51.792 --> 00:56:52.792
Don't do it for me…

997
00:56:55.250 --> 00:56:56.250
Do it for yourself.

998
00:57:00.375 --> 00:57:01.500
Take care.

999
00:57:02.875 --> 00:57:03.958
Jhinuk, I love you!

1000
00:57:04.625 --> 00:57:05.706
And I know you love me too.

1001
00:57:05.750 --> 00:57:07.917
I wouldn't insist if you were
truly happy here. Jhinuk!

1002
00:57:10.208 --> 00:57:11.583
College reunion?

1003
00:57:11.833 --> 00:57:13.633
What's even the point of going?
Waste of time.

1004
00:57:14.375 --> 00:57:16.250
People are just going to stand around

1005
00:57:16.333 --> 00:57:18.917
and boast about their lives.

1006
00:57:19.667 --> 00:57:21.375
No, my friends aren't like that.

1007
00:57:21.458 --> 00:57:23.139
You don't have to come, I'll go on my own.

1008
00:57:23.208 --> 00:57:24.208
On your own?

1009
00:57:24.292 --> 00:57:26.132
When was the last time
you went anywhere alone?

1010
00:57:27.583 --> 00:57:29.000
Have you ever given me the chance?

1011
00:57:29.167 --> 00:57:30.226
Don't make this bigger than it is.

1012
00:57:30.250 --> 00:57:31.490
You're not going, that's final.

1013
00:57:32.000 --> 00:57:33.875
Chumki's getting married in two months.

1014
00:57:33.958 --> 00:57:35.238
We've got a lot to take care of.

1015
00:57:39.167 --> 00:57:42.042
For centuries. Time and again.

1016
00:57:43.083 --> 00:57:44.375
This is what happens, my friend,

1017
00:57:44.792 --> 00:57:46.542
