Even though you're mine?</i>

1256
01:11:16.375 --> 01:11:19.208
<i>Tell me why?</i>

1257
01:11:21.917 --> 01:11:24.708
<i>-Teach me how to love you</i>
-Hold the lift.

1258
01:11:24.792 --> 01:11:25.792
Where are you going?

1259
01:11:26.375 --> 01:11:27.250
Grandma's house.

1260
01:11:27.333 --> 01:11:30.583
<i>Or teach me how to live without you</i>

1261
01:11:30.667 --> 01:11:32.042
Papa, your tag…

1262
01:11:32.542 --> 01:11:35.125
<i>-Why do you feel so far</i>
-Move!

1263
01:11:35.250 --> 01:11:37.667
<i>Even though you're mine?</i>

1264
01:11:37.750 --> 01:11:41.458
<i>- Tell me why?</i>
- Mom! What are you doing?!

1265
01:11:42.958 --> 01:11:46.917
<i>What about my heart?</i>

1266
01:11:47.208 --> 01:11:52.042
<i>What about my heart?</i>

1267
01:11:52.542 --> 01:11:58.917
<i>If your heart is a heart, then
My heart is also a heart, isn't it?</i>

1268
01:11:59.000 --> 01:12:00.042
Hello? Hi!

1269
01:12:00.125 --> 01:12:02.601
I'm just stepping out of the washroom.
I'll call you in two minutes.

1270
01:12:02.625 --> 01:12:03.792
Okay, bye-bye.

1271
01:12:04.417 --> 01:12:05.417
Bye.

1272
01:12:15.542 --> 01:12:16.542
Akash.

1273
01:12:25.375 --> 01:12:26.417
Where were you?

1274
01:12:26.958 --> 01:12:29.500
- Actually…
- You lied.

1275
01:12:31.042 --> 01:12:32.417
- No.
- You should've told me…

1276
01:12:34.208 --> 01:12:35.250
You were with him.

1277
01:12:35.833 --> 01:12:37.000
If I hadn't called,

1278
01:12:38.375 --> 01:12:39.816
you'd have spent the night with him.

1279
01:12:40.625 --> 01:12:42.226
- Akash!
- How long has this been going on?

1280
01:12:42.250 --> 01:12:43.500
What are you saying, Akash?

1281
01:12:43.667 --> 01:12:45.083
He's Parth, our…

1282
01:12:48.667 --> 01:12:50.000
What are you doing?

1283
01:12:50.125 --> 01:12:51.542
- Don't act…
- Listen.

1284
01:12:51.667 --> 01:12:52.708
- Stay out of this!
- Akash!

1285
01:12:52.792 --> 01:12:53.833
Listen to me.

1286
01:12:54.500 --> 01:12:55.542
- Get lost!
- Akash.

1287
01:12:57.250 --> 01:12:59.375
- I told you to stay out of this!
- You wanna fight?

1288
01:12:59.750 --> 01:13:00.875
- You...
- Best friend, my foot!

1289
01:13:00.958 --> 01:13:02.998
- You're not my friend! You jerk!
- Let him go, Akash!

1290
01:13:03.042 --> 01:13:04.208
You're sleeping with my wife!

1291
01:13:05.208 --> 01:13:06.250
What nonsense!

1292
01:13:06.333 --> 01:13:07.625
This is not nonsense.

1293
01:13:08.708 --> 01:13:10.029
I've been working hard in Mumbai.

1294
01:13:11.375 --> 01:13:13.583
And you two are just playing around here.

1295
01:13:14.000 --> 01:13:15.167
She's guilt-tripping me.

1296
01:13:15.792 --> 01:13:18.750
Guilt of long distance, sacrifice…

1297
01:13:22.542 --> 01:13:24.625
I don't even know if that baby was mine.

1298
01:13:28.708 --> 01:13:30.042
What are you trying to say?

1299
01:13:31.042 --> 01:13:32.833
Do you even know
what you're saying?

1300
01:13:32.917 --> 01:13:34.667
- I don't know.
- You have gone mad.

1301
01:13:36.208 --> 01:13:37.333
- You have gone crazy.
- What?

1302
01:13:37.417 --> 01:13:38.708
What did you just say?

1303
01:13:38.958 --> 01:13:40.167
Look at your state!

1304
01:13:42.458 --> 01:13:44.042
Don't freaking touch me!

1305
01:13:44.458 --> 01:13:45.458
Stay away!

1306
01:13:46.667 --> 01:13:48.917
You're blaming me?

1307
01:13:49.958 --> 01:13:51.500
I can't believe it!

1308
01:13:51.875 --> 01:13:53.458
First your Dad,

1309
01:13:54.083 --> 01:13:56.917
then Bombay, and now the baby.

1310
01:13:57.000 --> 01:14:01.083
You're going to blame the baby
that wasn't even born?

1311
01:14:04.542 --> 01:14:05.542
Let me go.

1312
01:14:09.208 --> 01:14:10.292
Once a loser,

1313
01:14:11.333 --> 01:14:12.333
always a loser.

1314
01:14:13.958 --> 01:14:17.458
You will die a failure.

1315
01:14:17.667 --> 01:14:22.708
<i>Why did you leave me?
Break me so carelessly?</i>

1316
01:14:22.792 --> 01:14:26.333
<i>I've fallen apart</i>

1317
01:14:28.250 --> 01:14:33.333
<i>My rotten luck took me away from you</i>

1318
01:14:33.500 --> 01:14:37.417
<i>Maybe there's something wrong with me</i>

1319
01:14:37.583 --> 01:14:41.167
<i>Why does every pore in me cry?</i>

1320
01:14:41.292 --> 01:14:42.875
<i>Why have I lost</i>

1321
01:14:42.958 --> 01:14:48.125
<i>Every reason to live and die?</i>

1322
01:14:48.250 --> 01:14:54.208
<i>Why have I carved you deep in my heart</i>

1323
01:14:54.958 --> 01:15:01.792
<i>I only wanted to make you mine
From the start</i>

1324
01:15:02.083 --> 01:15:03.208
I need to go to Mumbai.

1325
01:15:06.208 --> 01:15:07.708
I need to be with him.

1326
01:15:08.625 --> 01:15:09.792
Even after what he did today?

1327
01:15:10.083 --> 01:15:11.542
He crossed the line today, Shruti.

1328
01:15:11.625 --> 01:15:13.083
I crossed the line too.

1329
01:15:13.667 --> 01:15:14.958
We all do at some point.

1330
01:15:15.042 --> 01:15:16.583
That doesn't mean

1331
01:15:17.167 --> 01:15:18.958
we just give up on each other.

1332
01:15:20.042 --> 01:15:22.583
You two have such a toxic kind of love.
I just don't get it.

1333
01:15:24.000 --> 01:15:25.042
You won't get it.

1334
01:15:25.958 --> 01:15:28.083
- What?
- You won't understand.

1335
01:15:29.167 --> 01:15:30.208
Tell me,

1336
01:15:31.000 --> 01:15:33.625
what do you even know
about love and relationships?

1337
01:15:35.000 --> 01:15:36.708
- I know enough...
- You don't know anything.

1338
01:15:37.667 --> 01:15:38.958
And honestly,

1339
01:15:39.750 --> 01:15:41.311
I don't expect you
to understand either.

1340
01:15:57.875 --> 01:16:01.583
I've been knocking forever.
Why weren't you opening the door?

1341
01:16:03.292 --> 01:16:04.542
My jacket…

1342
01:16:05.625 --> 01:16:08.083
- Papa, are you drunk?
- Yes, I'm drunk.

1343
01:16:08.167 --> 01:16:09.167
So what?

1344
01:16:09.667 --> 01:16:12.125
Stop poking your nose into everything!

1345
01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:20.167
<i>Last time I saw you
You were right here</i>

1346
01:16:20.250 --> 01:16:25.333
<i>Then I turned around
And you were no longer there</i>

1347
01:16:25.625 --> 01:16:30.625
<i>Why can I not have you
After having you so close?</i>

1348
01:16:30.750 --> 01:16:33.667
<i>Can you please tell me?</i>

1349
01:16:36.208 --> 01:16:41.542
<i>Tell me how I should love you true</i>

1350
01:16:41.625 --> 01:16:46.917
<i>Or come and teach me how
To live without you</i>

1351
01:16:47.000 --> 01:16:52.042
<i>Why can I not have you
After having you so close?</i>

1352
01:16:52.125 --> 01:16:57.583
<i>Can you please tell me?</i>

1353
01:16:57.667 --> 01:17:02.833
<i>-I am lost, I am broken</i>
-Ma!

1354
01:17:02.958 --> 01:17:04.208
Is she upstairs?

1355
01:17:04.333 --> 01:17:08.292
<i>I feel like my soul's been silently stolen</i>

1356
01:17:08.375 --> 01:17:13.375
<i>I'm upset with myself, just like you</i>

1357
01:17:13.458 --> 01:17:17.458
<i>My story's almost through</i>

1358
01:17:17.542 --> 01:17:22.625
<i>You are going to leave anyway, too</i>

1359
01:17:22.792 --> 01:17:25.375
<i>What about this heart?</i>

1360
01:17:25.625 --> 01:17:28.000
<i>What about my heart?</i>

1361
01:17:28.167 --> 01:17:32.958
<i>If your heart is a heart, then</i>

1362
01:17:33.417 --> 01:17:40.375
<i>My heart is also a heart, is it not?</i>

1363
01:17:41.667 --> 01:17:46.458
<i>What about this heart?</i>

1364
01:17:46.833 --> 01:17:49.375
<i>What about my heart?</i>

1365
01:17:49.500 --> 01:17:54.625
<i>If your heart is a heart, then</i>

1366
01:17:54.750 --> 01:18:01.083
<i>My heart is also a heart, is it not?</i>

1367
01:18:05.542 --> 01:18:10.417
<i>What about my heart?</i>

1368
01:18:10.875 --> 01:18:15.542
<i>If your heart is a heart, then</i>

1369
01:18:16.000 --> 01:18:22.417
<i>My heart is also a heart, is it not?</i>

1370
01:18:24.375 --> 01:18:25.500
- Bye.
- Bye, Mom.

1371
01:18:25.583 --> 01:18:26.708
Love you.

1372
01:18:26.917 --> 01:18:28.292
- Have a safe trip.
- Hi, Papa!

1373
01:18:28.375 --> 01:18:29.375
Hi.

1374
01:18:31.167 --> 01:18:32.792
- I missed you, Papa.
- Missed you too.

1375
01:18:34.083 --> 01:18:34.958
- Bye.
- Bye.

1376
01:18:35.083 --> 01:18:36.542
- Bye!
- Go on, go.

1377
01:18:36.875 --> 01:18:38.333
- Bye!
- Bye!

1378
01:18:48.250 --> 01:18:49.625
Bro, he's right there.

1379
01:18:51.417 --> 01:18:55.083
Papa, you didn't visit Pune even once
in the past three months.

1380
01:18:55.417 --> 01:18:56.583
<i>I really missed you.</i>

1381
01:18:57.208 --> 01:18:58.750
<i>Papa, you're not trying your best.</i>

1382
01:18:59.542 --> 01:19:03.292
<i>If Mumma moves to Pune,
I'll have to change schools.</i>

1383
01:19:04.000 --> 01:19:05.333
When I come back,

1384
01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:08.292
promise me you both
will pick me up together. Okay?

1385
01:19:12.667 --> 01:19:13.667
You good?

1386
01:19:21.292 --> 01:19:22.292
Guddu.

1387
01:19:26.542 --> 01:19:28.667
Sir, sir, Akash Arya here.

1388
01:19:28.750 --> 01:19:29.750
Not now, afterwards.

1389
01:19:29.792 --> 01:19:30.851
- I'm a musician, sir.
- Afterwards.

1390
01:19:30.875 --> 01:19:32.500
- He said, "Not now."
- Sir, I…

1391
01:19:32.583 --> 01:19:34.144
Sir, just a minute. I'm not struggling.

1392
01:19:34.208 --> 01:19:35.542
- Why are you pushing me?
- Leave.

1393
01:19:35.708 --> 01:19:37.042
Get lost.

1394
01:19:46.375 --> 01:19:47.417
Hey.

1395
01:19:47.625 --> 01:19:49.785
I've got some sample invites.
Take a look and pick one.

1396
01:19:50.667 --> 01:19:52.809
- Baba, what's the rush? We'll do it later.
- Here you go.

1397
01:19:52.833 --> 01:19:54.458
- Biscuit?
- Biscuit?

1398
01:19:57.917 --> 01:19:58.792
Where's the biscuit?

1399
01:19:58.875 --> 01:20:01.542
Look, your father
isn't letting me go alone.

1400
01:20:01.625 --> 01:20:02.625
To Kolkata?

1401
01:20:02.667 --> 01:20:03.708
Baba, you choose.

1402
01:20:04.333 --> 01:20:06.333
Whatever you pick,
I'm sure it'll be perfect.

1403
01:20:10.458 --> 01:20:12.417
Hey, why don't you come with me?

1404
01:20:12.708 --> 01:20:13.917
It's just a small reunion.

1405
01:20:14.000 --> 01:20:17.458
We'll stay for a couple of days after that
and do some shopping.

1406
01:20:20.375 --> 01:20:21.375
Hey...

1407
01:20:22.750 --> 01:20:23.750
Hey.

1408
01:20:27.458 --> 01:20:28.333
You?

1409
01:20:28.417 --> 01:20:29.417
You?

1410
01:20:29.500 --> 01:20:30.500
You…

1411
01:20:30.625 --> 01:20:31.833
You're drenched.

1412
01:20:31.917 --> 01:20:33.018
- I'll get you a towel.
- Got drenched.

1413
01:20:33.042 --> 01:20:35.083
Monty? What are you doing here?

1414
01:20:35.625 --> 01:20:36.809
- Got drenched.
- Don't come inside.

1415
01:20:36.833 --> 01:20:37.708
- Listen to me.
- Please, leave.

1416
01:20:37.792 --> 01:20:39.726
- Listen to me. Just listen for a minute.
- Why should I? What is it?

1417
01:20:39.750 --> 01:20:41.671
- Talk to me in private. Just for a minute.
- Fine.

1418
01:20:41.750 --> 01:20:44.792
Wait, Baba, where are you going?
Finish your tea. Sit, please.

1419
01:20:44.875 --> 01:20:46.000
- Here.
- Finish your tea.

1420
01:20:46.250 --> 01:20:48.708
Why are you giving him a towel?
He's leaving.

1421
01:20:49.167 --> 01:20:50.417
If not for me,

1422
01:20:50.833 --> 01:20:52.042
then forgive me for you.

1423
01:20:53.042 --> 01:20:54.417
Look at the pain you're in.

1424
01:20:54.542 --> 01:20:55.833
I'm not in pain.

1425
01:20:55.917 --> 01:20:57.000
- You're not?
- No.

1426
01:20:57.875 --> 01:20:58.875
Well, I am.

1427
01:21:00.417 --> 01:21:01.917
I think I deserve a second chance.

1428
01:21:02.667 --> 01:21:03.667
What?

1429
01:21:04.083 --> 01:21:05.333
A second chance.

1430
01:21:05.417 --> 01:21:07.292
- A second chance? One minute.
- Hey…

1431
01:21:07.375 --> 01:21:08.375
Kajol…

1432
01:21:08.500 --> 01:21:09.375
What?

1433
01:21:09.458 --> 01:21:11.143
After everything you did?
You think you deserve a second chance?

1434
01:21:11.167 --> 01:21:12.434
You really think you deserve
one after all this?

1435
01:21:12.458 --> 01:21:13.375
No, no, Kajol, please…

1436
01:21:13.458 --> 01:21:14.476
Should I post this on the
WhatsApp group?

1437
01:21:14.500 --> 01:21:15.375
No, Kajol, don't.

1438
01:21:15.458 --> 01:21:16.559
- Chumki, come here.
- Come with me.

1439
01:21:16.583 --> 01:21:18.101
I want to show you
something very interesting.

1440
01:21:18.125 --> 01:21:19.000
Wait there.
Just stay right there.

1441
01:21:19.083 --> 01:21:19.958
Just hear him out.

1442
01:21:20.042 --> 01:21:21.601
- Ma, you don't even know what happened.
- Listen to him.

1443
01:21:21.625 --> 01:21:23.125
At least listen to him once.

1444
01:21:23.208 --> 01:21:24.226
- Why won't you listen?
- What?

1445
01:21:24.250 --> 01:21:25.250
What?

1446
01:21:25.833 --> 01:21:27.542
You're dragging this too far.

1447
01:21:27.625 --> 01:21:28.667
- Am I?
- Yes.

1448
01:21:29.750 --> 01:21:31.833
He admitted he was wrong.
He said sorry, right?

1449
01:21:31.958 --> 01:21:33.125
Give him another chance.

1450
01:21:33.958 --> 01:21:34.958
Wow.

1451
01:21:35.333 --> 01:21:36.454
That's exactly what he said,

1452
01:21:36.833 --> 01:21:38.042
"I deserve a second chance."

1453
01:21:38.125 --> 01:21:39.833
And now you're siding with him.

1454
01:21:39.917 --> 01:21:40.917
He's not wrong.

1455
01:21:41.500 --> 01:21:43.000
In marriage, you have to adjust.

1456
01:21:43.083 --> 01:21:44.083
That's just how it is.

1457
01:21:47.375 --> 01:21:48.458
Oh, like you did?

1458
01:21:52.583 --> 01:21:54.000
By giving Baba a second chance?

1459
01:21:57.750 --> 01:22:01.708
You think I don't know
about Auntie Sheila?

1460
01:22:06.542 --> 01:22:08.667
I was in tenth grade

1461
01:22:09.292 --> 01:22:11.333
when you found out about his affair.

1462
01:22:12.292 --> 01:22:13.292
And so did I.

1463
01:22:13.958 --> 01:22:16.333
For a whole year, every other day,

1464
01:22:16.458 --> 01:22:18.143
you'd lock yourself
in the bathroom and cry.

1465
01:22:18.167 --> 01:22:21.708
And I'd turn up the TV volume
so Chumki wouldn't hear you.

1466
01:22:23.792 --> 01:22:26.875
You didn't have the courage
to leave him.

1467
01:22:26.958 --> 01:22:28.083
Or leave the house.

1468
01:22:39.125 --> 01:22:40.542
Chumki was just four.

1469
01:22:42.500 --> 01:22:45.417
You both were so young, so I…

1470
01:22:45.667 --> 01:22:47.083
For the sake of the kids, I…

1471
01:22:47.250 --> 01:22:51.333
How long are you going
to keep hiding behind that excuse?

1472
01:22:53.083 --> 01:22:56.333
At least now admit it
that you never had the courage.

1473
01:22:57.667 --> 01:22:59.583
You know, I never wanted
to turn out like you.

1474
01:23:02.083 --> 01:23:04.042
But that's exactly who I've become.

1475
01:23:05.500 --> 01:23:07.458
All I think about is family.

1476
01:23:07.667 --> 01:23:10.333
I have no goals, no dreams,
nothing of my own.

1477
01:23:10.625 --> 01:23:12.706
I was supposed to spend my life as a
happy housewife.

1478
01:23:13.542 --> 01:23:14.542
Why?

1479
01:23:15.042 --> 01:23:17.083
Because marriage means
adjusting, right?

1480
01:23:19.125 --> 01:23:20.667
I've become a doormat just like you,

1481
01:23:20.750 --> 01:23:22.417
and I hate myself for it!

1482
01:23:25.208 --> 01:23:27.226
You're getting married, right?
Well, this is what marriage looks like.

1483
01:23:27.250 --> 01:23:28.333
Congratulations.

1484
01:23:43.333 --> 01:23:45.083
The fetus is 18 weeks old.

1485
01:23:45.500 --> 01:23:47.708
And by this time, they start
developing very quickly.

1486
01:23:48.458 --> 01:23:51.750
Frankly, you should've made
the decision to terminate long ago.

1487
01:23:54.208 --> 01:23:55.292
I tried…

1488
01:23:58.000 --> 01:23:59.160
Just didn't have the courage.

1489
01:23:59.667 --> 01:24:01.500
<i>You don't have enough time.</i>

1490
01:24:02.333 --> 01:24:04.125
<i>One to two weeks.
Maximum.</i>

1491
01:24:05.167 --> 01:24:07.333
<i>I would say, discuss it with your family.</i>

1492
01:24:07.417 --> 01:24:08.708
<i>Whatever the decision is,</i>

1493
01:24:09.000 --> 01:24:10.667
<i>just make very sure it's your choice.</i>

1494
01:24:17.208 --> 01:24:19.000
I…

1495
01:24:20.875 --> 01:24:21.750
One second.

1496
01:24:21.833 --> 01:24:23.194
One second, just a second, Shruti.

1497
01:24:23.667 --> 01:24:24.542
Hello?

1498
01:24:24.667 --> 01:24:26.833
Yes, sir. Yes, sir. I'm here.

1499
01:24:26.917 --> 01:24:27.792
Hello?

1500
01:24:27.875 --> 01:24:30.000
No, sir, please don't say that.

1501
01:24:30.500 --> 01:24:31.792
Sir, please.

1502
01:24:31.875 --> 01:24:34.833
Just please listen to it once more.

1503
01:24:34.958 --> 01:24:36.042
It's only a raw mix.

1504
01:24:36.167 --> 01:24:39.875
I'll rework it tonight
and send you a new version.

1505
01:24:39.958 --> 01:24:41.375
Sir, please. Please, sir.

1506
01:24:41.542 --> 01:24:42.643
Instruments are not added yet.

1507
01:24:42.667 --> 01:24:44.417
It's just a matter of…
a few tweaks.

1508
01:24:51.708 --> 01:24:52.749
You were saying something?

1509
01:24:56.750 --> 01:24:57.875
No, it's nothing.

1510
01:25:18.708 --> 01:25:19.708
Kajol,

1511
01:25:20.583 --> 01:25:23.458
when a relationship
has lasted for years,

1512
01:25:25.417 --> 01:25:26.617
things like this… they happen.

1513
01:25:27.250 --> 01:25:28.250
I…

1514
01:25:29.042 --> 01:25:30.667
I understand your situation.

1515
01:25:31.792 --> 01:25:32.792
Really, Baba?

1516
01:25:33.833 --> 01:25:35.667
You were on the other side
of this situation.

1517
01:25:36.875 --> 01:25:37.875
Right?

1518
01:25:41.042 --> 01:25:42.667
All these years, you've…

1519
01:25:46.375 --> 01:25:48.125
You've hated me all these years.

1520
01:25:49.417 --> 01:25:50.708
No, I deserve it, but…

1521
01:25:53.083 --> 01:25:54.458
But you never made me feel it.

1522
01:25:55.708 --> 01:25:56.958
I made a mistake.

1523
01:25:57.958 --> 01:25:59.208
A blunder, actually.

1524
01:26:02.458 --> 01:26:03.458
Monty…

1525
01:26:06.458 --> 01:26:07.458
Monty!

1526
01:26:09.250 --> 01:26:10.250
Wait, please.

1527
01:26:12.125 --> 01:26:16.750
Your mother gave me just one chance
to make things right.

1528
01:26:18.333 --> 01:26:21.625
Despite what I did to her.

1529
01:26:26.375 --> 01:26:28.583
She's the only woman
I've ever truly loved.

1530
01:26:30.208 --> 01:26:31.208
You,

1531
01:26:31.458 --> 01:26:32.458
Chumki,

1532
01:26:33.333 --> 01:26:34.333
your mother…

1533
01:26:34.625 --> 01:26:37.750
You're my whole world.
My everything.

1534
01:26:48.333 --> 01:26:49.542
For the first time,

1535
01:26:50.292 --> 01:26:51.452
I'm asking you for something.

1536
01:26:54.708 --> 01:26:57.583
Why don't you go away
for a few days?

1537
01:26:57.708 --> 01:26:59.792
- You know, to talk this through.
- Oh, please.

1538
01:26:59.917 --> 01:27:01.583
Try to sort it out.

1539
01:27:02.292 --> 01:27:04.583
Falling out of love is normal.

1540
01:27:06.292 --> 01:27:07.500
It happens to everyone.

1541
01:27:08.750 --> 01:27:10.000
But no one talks about it.

1542
01:27:11.708 --> 01:27:12.792
That's why,

1543
01:27:13.708 --> 01:27:15.875
in a marriage,
you've got to choose to fall in love

1544
01:27:16.583 --> 01:27:17.958
with the same person…

1545
01:27:20.250 --> 01:27:22.417
Over and over again.

1546
01:27:24.333 --> 01:27:27.417
That's the only way it lasts.

1547
01:27:28.083 --> 01:27:29.083
Please,

1548
01:27:29.958 --> 01:27:32.250
just give it a try.

1549
01:27:33.750 --> 01:27:34.750
Honestly.

1550
01:27:36.917 --> 01:27:39.250
And if it still doesn't work…

1551
01:27:42.292 --> 01:27:44.833
I'll get you a lawyer.
I'll help you get a divorce.

1552
01:27:46.875 --> 01:27:50.375
But, sweetheart, just one last try.

1553
01:27:51.667 --> 01:27:52.667
Please.

1554
01:28:06.917 --> 01:28:09.708
I'm sorry. I lied to you.

1555
01:28:10.625 --> 01:28:14.458
I've done this maybe three, four…

1556
01:28:15.458 --> 01:28:18.042
Actually, six, no, seven times.

1557
01:28:18.750 --> 01:28:20.625
But I never crossed the line.

1558
01:28:20.917 --> 01:28:22.042
There was just one time

1559
01:28:22.125 --> 01:28:24.125
she kissed me near my lips,
not on them.

1560
01:28:24.208 --> 01:28:26.042
- Stop the car!
- Don't yell!

1561
01:28:26.125 --> 01:28:27.184
I only got caught because of you.

1562
01:28:27.208 --> 01:28:28.643
- I said, "Stop the car!"
- You set a honey trap!

1563
01:28:28.667 --> 01:28:29.768
If it wasn't for that,
I would have never been caught.

1564
01:28:29.792 --> 01:28:30.851
You have the nerve to say that!

1565
01:28:30.875 --> 01:28:32.958
Unknowingly, I was getting
attracted to you again.

1566
01:28:33.125 --> 01:28:34.750
Bullshit! Pervert!

1567
01:28:34.917 --> 01:28:36.500
Rotten values, disgusting upbringing.

1568
01:28:36.625 --> 01:28:38.292
Oh, and your dad's not a pervert?

1569
01:28:38.500 --> 01:28:40.458
How dare you bring up my dad?
How dare you!

1570
01:28:40.542 --> 01:28:42.292
You stop the car!
Stop the car!

1571
01:28:42.375 --> 01:28:43.726
It was a mistake, Kajol.
Both me and your dad made mistakes.

1572
01:28:43.750 --> 01:28:44.768
- You call it a mistake?
- Yes.

1573
01:28:44.792 --> 01:28:46.667
Seven times?
The same mistake, seven times?

1574
01:28:46.750 --> 01:28:47.667
Haven't you ever made a mistake?

1575
01:28:47.750 --> 01:28:49.030
What mistake?
Tell me what I did!

1576
01:28:49.083 --> 01:28:51.351
Remember when your friend
from London came and you met him?

1577
01:28:51.375 --> 01:28:52.726
You're seriously bringing up
college right now?

1578
01:28:52.750 --> 01:28:54.559
- Something that happened ten years ago?
- Yeah. So?

1579
01:28:54.583 --> 01:28:56.184
You're just digging that up
to justify what you did!

1580
01:28:56.208 --> 01:28:57.226
I didn't follow you back then.

1581
01:28:57.250 --> 01:28:58.601
Otherwise, you would've
been caught too.

1582
01:28:58.625 --> 01:29:00.018
- What were you doing for four hours?
- Just to justify your mistake.

1583
01:29:00.042 --> 01:29:01.542
We had dinner! Just dinner!

1584
01:29:01.625 --> 01:29:04.208
Listen, I don't want to listen!
Stop the car or I swear…

1585
01:29:04.292 --> 01:29:05.458
- Or I will jump!
- Stop! No!

1586
01:29:05.542 --> 01:29:06.667
Stop the car now!

1587
01:29:09.458 --> 01:29:10.458
Ma?

1588
01:29:12.208 --> 01:29:13.292
Ma, I'm going.

1589
01:29:15.833 --> 01:29:16.833
Ma!

1590
01:29:19.542 --> 01:29:23.083
<i>Sanjeev, I want to be alone for a while.</i>

1591
01:29:24.833 --> 01:29:28.833
<i>I'm going to the reunion.
I'll be back in two days.</i>

1592
01:29:29.292 --> 01:29:30.833
<i>As I usually come back.</i>

1593
01:29:32.625 --> 01:29:33.625
I'm off, Baba.

1594
01:29:34.042 --> 01:29:36.442
<i>There were times you didn't answer
my calls for a whole week.</i>

1595
01:29:37.083 --> 01:29:39.458
<i>I'm sure you can manage
two days without me.</i>

1596
01:29:40.167 --> 01:29:41.583
<i>I keep hearing from the kids.</i>

1597
01:29:41.708 --> 01:29:44.083
<i>Space.</i>

1598
01:29:44.792 --> 01:29:46.583
<i>Maybe that's what I need right now.</i>

1599
01:29:47.333 --> 01:29:48.333
<i>Shibani.</i>

1600
01:30:06.333 --> 01:30:07.917
- Drive next to her.
- Okay.

1601
01:30:08.875 --> 01:30:11.208
- Shall I help you, madam?
- I don't want it. Get going.

1602
01:30:11.292 --> 01:30:13.125
- It must be heavy.
- Get lost.

1603
01:30:13.292 --> 01:30:14.292
Hey!

1604
01:30:14.583 --> 01:30:15.750
- Hey!
- Fools!

1605
01:30:19.250 --> 01:30:22.583
- Kajol, come on, get in the car.
- I am fine.

1606
01:30:22.833 --> 01:30:23.917
It's getting dark.

1607
01:30:24.042 --> 01:30:26.000
You can be mad at me
even while sitting inside.

1608
01:30:32.875 --> 01:30:33.875
Ms. Maya?

1609
01:30:34.500 --> 01:30:35.833
Is that really you, Ms. Maya?

1610
01:30:36.000 --> 01:30:37.417
Oh, my God, I thought so.

1611
01:30:37.708 --> 01:30:39.292
You didn't recognize me?

1612
01:30:39.417 --> 01:30:41.042
I'm Wing Commander Raina.

1613
01:30:41.583 --> 01:30:43.768
Please get in, I'll drop you home.
Come on, let me drop you off at home.

1614
01:30:43.792 --> 01:30:45.667
I don't talk to strangers, sorry.

1615
01:30:47.167 --> 01:30:50.625
Sometimes you can tell strangers
the things you can't tell your loved ones.

1616
01:30:51.042 --> 01:30:52.962
Remember, you texted me
something like that once?

1617
01:30:54.125 --> 01:30:56.000
Two strangers on a path unknown,

1618
01:30:56.208 --> 01:30:58.250
by the end,
we'll surely have a tale to tell.

1619
01:30:58.917 --> 01:30:59.917
Please, come.

1620
01:31:02.125 --> 01:31:03.125
Please, get in.

1621
01:31:06.875 --> 01:31:07.875
Come on.

1622
01:31:26.125 --> 01:31:27.125
Kajol?

1623
01:31:27.875 --> 01:31:28.875
Kajol?

1624
01:31:30.750 --> 01:31:31.750
Ms. Maya?

1625
01:31:34.708 --> 01:31:35.708
Tea.

1626
01:31:38.667 --> 01:31:40.417
Could I have some water, Mr. Raina?

1627
01:31:41.167 --> 01:31:42.927
I'll make it rain for you,
just say the word!

1628
01:31:44.458 --> 01:31:48.833
Wow, a miracle!
I'll get it for you right now.

1629
01:31:48.917 --> 01:31:51.583
- Wait here, I'll bring the water.
- Bring water.

1630
01:31:55.333 --> 01:31:57.042
Hey, Kajol?

1631
01:31:57.583 --> 01:31:58.583
Kajol!

1632
01:31:59.667 --> 01:32:00.667
Kajol!

1633
01:32:30.333 --> 01:32:32.083
Babita, my God!

1634
01:32:32.250 --> 01:32:33.458
I'll give it. No, not yet.

1635
01:32:33.542 --> 01:32:35.708
After so long. Come.
Come here, come here.

1636
01:32:35.792 --> 01:32:37.292
My hero, Parimal.

1637
01:32:37.375 --> 01:32:38.917
- Look who's here.
- How are you?

1638
01:32:39.083 --> 01:32:40.667
Who'll listen to my stories now?

1639
01:32:40.750 --> 01:32:41.958
Wow! Look who's here!

1640
01:32:42.042 --> 01:32:43.667
- Bani!
- Bani!

1641
01:32:43.792 --> 01:32:45.500
Back in the day…

1642
01:32:45.583 --> 01:32:46.708
Come on.

1643
01:32:47.208 --> 01:32:49.958
Now, if you could please sing
our beloved "Majnu" anthem!

1644
01:32:50.042 --> 01:32:51.667
- Oh yes!
- Yes, yes!

1645
01:32:53.750 --> 01:32:55.958
- Stop it, it's been 40 years.
- Please sing.

1646
01:32:56.042 --> 01:32:57.792
I don't remember it.

1647
01:32:57.875 --> 01:32:59.101
You will have to recite it today.

1648
01:32:59.125 --> 01:33:00.958
I don't remember it.
Please!

1649
01:33:23.125 --> 01:33:25.042
Hey, I'm so sorry.

1650
01:33:25.333 --> 01:33:26.333
Are you alright?

1651
01:33:27.167 --> 01:33:28.083
Please tell me you're okay.

1652
01:33:28.167 --> 01:33:29.750
I'm so sorry, I'm so sorry.

1653
01:33:32.208 --> 01:33:37.583
<i>Our eyes have been talking
To each other for eternity</i>

1654
01:33:38.708 --> 01:33:44.500
<i>The movement of our eyelashes begins
To reveal secrets</i>

1655
01:33:44.583 --> 01:33:47.333
<i>Don't ask me about
The condition of my heart</i>

1656
01:33:48.167 --> 01:33:52.000
<i>Day and night, it just wants to</i>

1657
01:33:52.208 --> 01:33:55.792
<i>Love, love, love you. Only you</i>

1658
01:33:55.875 --> 01:33:57.542
Come on, Parimal!

1659
01:33:58.250 --> 01:33:59.125
I don't know.

1660
01:33:59.208 --> 01:34:00.458
We'll sing along.

1661
01:34:00.542 --> 01:34:01.417
Yeah!

1662
01:34:01.500 --> 01:34:02.708
Come on!

1663
01:34:10.125 --> 01:34:15.042
<i>Why love, love, love?
Pointless love</i>

1664
01:34:16.917 --> 01:34:18.667
<i>Even my secrets</i>

1665
01:34:18.750 --> 01:34:19.750
You okay?

1666
01:34:22.042 --> 01:34:23.042
Aryan.

1667
01:34:23.458 --> 01:34:24.458
I'm Maya.

1668
01:34:25.000 --> 01:34:26.250
Maya.

1669
01:34:26.542 --> 01:34:28.333
-Maya
-Hi.

1670
01:34:29.958 --> 01:34:32.042
<i>We'll think about tomorrow when it comes</i>

1671
01:34:33.000 --> 01:34:35.958
<i>From afar, why don't we just</i>

1672
01:34:36.083 --> 01:34:40.583
<i>Love, love, love. Pointless love</i>

1673
01:34:42.167 --> 01:34:46.958
<i>My heart loves, loves, loves only you</i>

1674
01:35:07.583 --> 01:35:11.333
<i>Life moves so swiftly</i>

1675
01:35:12.250 --> 01:35:16.958
<i>Come sit with me for another cup of tea</i>

1676
01:35:17.292 --> 01:35:21.333
<i>Life moves so swiftly</i>

1677
01:35:21.792 --> 01:35:26.167
<i>Come sit with me for another cup of tea</i>

1678
01:35:26.833 --> 01:35:31.625
<i>I've had a bypass, my sugar's high</i>

1679
01:35:31.750 --> 01:35:34.083
<i>I eat, sleep, wake up, and live all alone</i>

1680
01:35:34.167 --> 01:35:36.208
<i>My boat's got two holes
And is sinking slowly</i>

1681
01:35:36.292 --> 01:35:39.458
<i>My "oh wow" turned to "oh no"</i>

1682
01:35:40.958 --> 01:35:44.250
<i>My tool's rusted and worn</i>

1683
01:35:44.333 --> 01:35:45.458
Shut up.

1684
01:35:46.208 --> 01:35:48.667
<i>Now I share my feelings
With my old buddies</i>

1685
01:35:48.750 --> 01:35:51.125
<i>And each one revealing
Tales of grief untold</i>

1686
01:35:51.208 --> 01:35:54.917
<i>Life moves so swiftly</i>

1687
01:35:55.625 --> 01:35:59.583
<i>Come sit with me for another cup of tea</i>

1688
01:36:01.167 --> 01:36:02.750
Bani, how about you?

1689
01:36:05.417 --> 01:36:10.208
<i>I stayed at home like
A pocket handkerchief, quiet</i>

1690
01:36:10.333 --> 01:36:14.958
<i>Every day, I played the roles
Of mother and wife</i>

1691
01:36:15.458 --> 01:36:19.750
<i>My household became my joy and pride</i>

1692
01:36:20.208 --> 01:36:24.667
<i>I lost myself in the routine of life</i>

1693
01:36:25.333 --> 01:36:29.500
<i>Though I have everything for sure</i>

1694
01:36:29.917 --> 01:36:32.083
<i>I still wish and crave more</i>

1695
01:36:32.375 --> 01:36:35.000
<i>But maybe that's not in store</i>

1696
01:36:35.125 --> 01:36:38.708
<i>Life moves so swiftly</i>

1697
01:36:39.667 --> 01:36:43.667
<i>Come sit with me for another cup of tea</i>

1698
01:36:44.542 --> 01:36:49.083
<i>We loved to shop, the four of us</i>

1699
01:36:49.292 --> 01:36:53.833
<i>Sudha, my son, his wife, and I
Oh, those days were a plus</i>

1700
01:36:54.125 --> 01:36:58.625
<i>One day, the four of us split into
Two rickshaws</i>

1701
01:36:58.958 --> 01:37:00.917
<i>Sudha with Aabir</i>

1702
01:37:01.292 --> 01:37:03.708
<i>My daughter-in-law with me
To make us all fit</i>

1703
01:37:04.542 --> 01:37:08.375
<i>A truck broke the divider
Reckless and rash</i>

1704
01:37:08.625 --> 01:37:13.333
<i>It slammed the front rickshaw
With a thunderous crash</i>

1705
01:37:13.417 --> 01:37:14.833
<i>Sudha was killed on the spot</i>

1706
01:37:15.625 --> 01:37:17.833
<i>My son, on the way to the hospital</i>

1707
01:37:19.542 --> 01:37:21.583
<i>An old man left alone to roam</i>

1708
01:37:22.667 --> 01:37:24.458
<i>A young girl widowed far from home</i>

1709
01:37:27.542 --> 01:37:31.167
<i>Why did such a thing have to happen</i>

1710
01:37:31.875 --> 01:37:35.500
<i>I can't say</i>

1711
01:37:36.708 --> 01:37:40.125
<i>We used to make four cups of tea</i>

1712
01:37:40.875 --> 01:37:46.292
<i>Now just two each day</i>

1713
01:37:57.792 --> 01:38:00.432
This is a new initiative I've started.
A theater workshop for kids.

1714
01:38:00.875 --> 01:38:01.875
Nice.

1715
01:38:04.833 --> 01:38:05.833
I'm getting married.

1716
01:38:08.875 --> 01:38:09.875
What?

1717
01:38:10.083 --> 01:38:11.417
People change, and so have I.

1718
01:38:13.333 --> 01:38:14.375
Just like that?

1719
01:38:15.000 --> 01:38:16.000
Just like that.

1720
01:38:17.042 --> 01:38:18.042
Love marriage?

1721
01:38:18.833 --> 01:38:20.292
Love can happen after marriage, too.

1722
01:38:21.500 --> 01:38:24.208
She owns a boutique cafe in Shimla.

1723
01:38:25.167 --> 01:38:27.087
She'll manage the boutique.
I'll handle the cafe.

1724
01:38:27.958 --> 01:38:28.958
So sorted. See.

1725
01:38:29.667 --> 01:38:30.667
Now tell me…

1726
01:38:31.500 --> 01:38:34.292
You said love is the main course,
and the rest is all dessert.

1727
01:38:35.250 --> 01:38:37.083
For her, I'd skip dessert altogether.

1728
01:38:37.792 --> 01:38:39.083
- For her?
- Baby!

1729
01:38:39.167 --> 01:38:40.583
You want to…

1730
01:38:41.208 --> 01:38:43.167
- Actually, no, wait, wait, wait.
- Yeah.

1731
01:38:44.208 --> 01:38:45.458
Hi, baby.

1732
01:39:12.708 --> 01:39:16.458
I'm staying in a rented
apartment in London, uncle.

1733
01:39:17.083 --> 01:39:18.684
I plan to buy my own house in two years.

1734
01:39:20.000 --> 01:39:22.417
So, you're well settled there.

1735
01:39:22.875 --> 01:39:23.875
Yes.

1736
01:39:24.583 --> 01:39:27.417
You know, when you,
Aabir, and Jhinuk were in college,

1737
01:39:27.500 --> 01:39:33.125
I could never tell
if Jhinuk loved you or Aabir.

1738
01:39:33.208 --> 01:39:37.083
No, Uncle, there was nothing like
that between Jhinuk and me.

1739
01:39:37.167 --> 01:39:39.125
- I know, I know.
- We are just good friends.

1740
01:39:46.208 --> 01:39:48.000
I had a girlfriend in college.

1741
01:39:50.000 --> 01:39:52.583
She wanted to wait for me,
but I didn't stop her.

1742
01:39:53.208 --> 01:39:54.208
I let her go.

1743
01:39:54.875 --> 01:39:57.875
Just like you're waiting for Jhinuk,

1744
01:39:58.042 --> 01:40:01.458
and she can't gather the courage
to commit, just like me.

1745
01:40:05.542 --> 01:40:07.042
I know I'm the reason.

1746
01:40:07.750 --> 01:40:08.750
Am I right?

1747
01:40:10.833 --> 01:40:11.833
Uncle,

1748
01:40:14.750 --> 01:40:15.750
Aabir...

1749
01:40:16.750 --> 01:40:17.833
Uncle, before he left us…

1750
01:40:17.958 --> 01:40:20.708
You mean before his death?

1751
01:40:26.000 --> 01:40:28.250
Aabir told Jhinuk…

1752
01:40:29.792 --> 01:40:31.125
To always take care of you.

1753
01:40:32.042 --> 01:40:33.500
That she shouldn't leave you alone.

1754
01:40:34.417 --> 01:40:36.417
Aabir's last words are etched
into Jhinuk's mind,

1755
01:40:36.500 --> 01:40:39.208
and they won't leave.

1756
01:40:40.208 --> 01:40:41.689
Then we'll have to get them out, son.

1757
01:40:42.792 --> 01:40:46.167
Otherwise, neither Jhinuk,
nor you, nor I will be happy.

1758
01:40:46.875 --> 01:40:50.125
So keep meeting and talking to her.

1759
01:40:50.875 --> 01:40:52.208
You love her, right?

1760
01:40:53.542 --> 01:40:54.542
Then have some courage.

1761
01:40:55.458 --> 01:40:56.458
Have patience.

1762
01:40:57.167 --> 01:40:59.417
I'm already trying.
You should keep trying, too.

1763
01:41:07.125 --> 01:41:09.000
- Hey, dear.
<i>- Hi, Papa.</i>

1764
01:41:09.417 --> 01:41:11.417
Where is Mumma?

1765
01:41:13.000 --> 01:41:14.000
Darling…

1766
01:41:15.208 --> 01:41:16.583
She's in the washroom.

1767
01:41:17.583 --> 01:41:20.417
Where are you guys staying,
North Goa or South?

1768
01:41:20.500 --> 01:41:21.542
Of course, South.

1769
01:41:25.250 --> 01:41:26.458
Okay, Papa, I have to go. Bye.

1770
01:41:32.625 --> 01:41:34.000
And here we are.

1771
01:41:36.542 --> 01:41:38.167
- I had fun.
- Thanks.

1772
01:41:38.292 --> 01:41:39.875
So, let's meet tomorrow morning?

1773
01:41:40.333 --> 01:41:41.333
- Tomorrow? Again?
- Yeah.

1774
01:41:41.500 --> 01:41:43.000
Thought I'd show you around a bit.

1775
01:41:43.792 --> 01:41:46.208
Actually, I'm busy tomorrow, so…

1776
01:41:46.750 --> 01:41:49.125
- Okay, I got it, yeah.
- Okay.

1777
01:41:50.083 --> 01:41:51.083
- Bye.
- Bye.

1778
01:41:54.292 --> 01:41:59.125
Actually, we can meet
for breakfast tomorrow, if you want.

1779
01:42:00.292 --> 01:42:01.167
At 09:30 a.m.?

1780
01:42:01.250 --> 01:42:02.292
- Bye.
- Bye.

1781
01:42:06.708 --> 01:42:07.708
Pihu!

1782
01:42:07.875 --> 01:42:10.000
Wow, Mom, you look so pretty!

1783
01:42:10.167 --> 01:42:12.333
- Really? You really think so?
- Yes.

1784
01:42:12.417 --> 01:42:13.417
Anyway, are you alright?

1785
01:42:15.833 --> 01:42:17.042
Where are you guys staying?

1786
01:42:17.167 --> 01:42:18.167
North or South?

1787
01:42:18.250 --> 01:42:19.292
North.

1788
01:42:20.208 --> 01:42:21.208
- Hi.
- Hi.

1789
01:42:21.333 --> 01:42:22.667
Where's Papa?

1790
01:42:23.333 --> 01:42:25.833
<i>He's gone to the petrol pump.
He'll be back soon.</i>

1791
01:42:26.125 --> 01:42:27.846
<i>- Listen, are you eating enough...</i>
- Okay, bye.

1792
01:42:41.208 --> 01:42:42.208
Thank you, sir.

1793
01:42:43.458 --> 01:42:44.458
Hello.

1794
01:42:50.292 --> 01:42:51.875
So you didn't tell anyone?

1795
01:42:52.625 --> 01:42:54.000
Only my youngest daughter knows.

1796
01:42:54.333 --> 01:42:55.333
Why?

1797
01:42:56.750 --> 01:42:57.750
I just decided not to.

1798
01:43:00.500 --> 01:43:01.750
Running away at this age?

1799
01:43:03.917 --> 01:43:06.583
I've thought about running away
many times before.

1800
01:43:08.125 --> 01:43:09.417
This time, I actually did it.

1801
01:43:11.417 --> 01:43:12.542
You're quite something.

1802
01:43:13.833 --> 01:43:15.083
He must be worried sick.

1803
01:43:19.500 --> 01:43:20.875
His name is Sanjeev.

1804
01:43:22.875 --> 01:43:24.167
Let him worry a bit.

1805
01:43:26.250 --> 01:43:27.667
I gave him 40 years,

1806
01:43:28.875 --> 01:43:31.000
can't he spare me 40 hours?

1807
01:43:33.958 --> 01:43:36.479
You may have wrinkles now,
but you're still just as mischievous.

1808
01:43:39.500 --> 01:43:41.500
You should leave soon,
the airport's far from here.

1809
01:43:44.708 --> 01:43:46.375
Are you really going
to let me go again?

1810
01:43:49.292 --> 01:43:51.500
Don't worry, I'm leaving, I promise.

1811
01:43:51.958 --> 01:43:53.439
What's the point of stopping you now?

1812
01:43:54.208 --> 01:43:56.708
Neither our youth remains, nor that city.

1813
01:43:59.125 --> 01:44:00.458
The city looks the same,

1814
01:44:02.417 --> 01:44:04.042
but maybe we've changed.

1815
01:44:05.833 --> 01:44:06.833
Maybe.

1816
01:44:07.417 --> 01:44:09.292
Age is just a number, Parimal.

1817
01:44:11.250 --> 01:44:14.875
If you forget to count for a day,
I'll forget my flight.

1818
01:44:44.583 --> 01:44:48.167
<i>I like the weather in your city</i>

1819
01:44:48.500 --> 01:44:51.917
<i>It's so fine</i>

1820
01:44:52.292 --> 01:44:56.083
<i>Let me steal an evening</i>

1821
01:44:56.375 --> 01:45:00.083
<i>If you don't mind</i>

1822
01:45:00.333 --> 01:45:04.458
<i>If you can forget me</i>

1823
01:45:04.542 --> 01:45:07.792
<i>Then go on, be free</i>

1824
01:45:08.167 --> 01:45:12.625
<i>But to forget you</i>

1825
01:45:12.750 --> 01:45:15.708
<i>Might take a lifetime for me</i>

1826
01:45:16.042 --> 01:45:19.708
<i>Might take a lifetime</i>

1827
01:45:19.917 --> 01:45:23.750
<i>For me</i>

1828
01:45:23.958 --> 01:45:27.583
<i>To forget you</i>

1829
01:45:27.667 --> 01:45:31.708
<i>Might take a lifetime for me</i>

1830
01:45:31.792 --> 01:45:35.458
<i>Might take a lifetime</i>

1831
01:45:35.708 --> 01:45:39.542
<i>For me</i>

1832
01:45:39.667 --> 01:45:42.500
<i>To forget you</i>

1833
01:45:43.625 --> 01:45:47.042
<i>Might take a lifetime for me</i>

1834
01:45:47.125 --> 01:45:48.042
Where could Ma possibly go?

1835
01:45:48.125 --> 01:45:49.750
But how do I contact her?

1836
01:45:50.083 --> 01:45:51.601
Okay, I'm not supposed to tell you this,

1837
01:45:51.625 --> 01:45:54.042
but she took my spare phone with her.

1838
01:45:54.625 --> 01:45:55.865
<i>So you can just call her there.</i>

1839
01:45:55.958 --> 01:45:57.417
I already tried that.

1840
01:45:57.792 --> 01:45:59.417
She has blocked me.

1841
01:46:00.042 --> 01:46:01.125
<i>Who does that?</i>

1842
01:46:01.292 --> 01:46:04.917
<i>Baba, I'm just saying
what you told Kajol.</i>

1843
01:46:06.042 --> 01:46:09.625
You have to fall in love
with the same person again and again.

1844
01:46:10.917 --> 01:46:11.917
<i>Give it a try.</i>

1845
01:46:12.750 --> 01:46:13.750
Go, find her.

1846
01:46:13.958 --> 01:46:16.292
<i>Track her friends, her college…</i>

1847
01:46:16.500 --> 01:46:17.833
<i>locate her phone.</i>

1848
01:46:18.417 --> 01:46:21.625
Just woo her again, Baba.

1849
01:46:21.750 --> 01:46:22.750
Okay.

1850
01:46:22.958 --> 01:46:25.625
Or your second option is
to just give her space.

1851
01:46:25.875 --> 01:46:26.875
What?

1852
01:46:31.208 --> 01:46:37.917
<i>I admit it this time
The fault was mine</i>

1853
01:46:39.167 --> 01:46:44.917
<i>The one who once loved me</i>

1854
01:46:46.417 --> 01:46:50.167
<i>Now draws a hard line</i>

1855
01:46:50.375 --> 01:46:54.792
<i>Don't be so harsh
There's pain you can't see</i>

1856
01:46:54.958 --> 01:47:01.625
<i>My heart keeps aching endlessly</i>

1857
01:47:02.292 --> 01:47:06.417
<i>If you must betray me</i>

1858
01:47:06.583 --> 01:47:09.917
<i>Do it so true</i>

1859
01:47:10.125 --> 01:47:14.333
<i>If you must betray me</i>

1860
01:47:14.417 --> 01:47:17.792
<i>Do it so true</i>

1861
01:47:18.042 --> 01:47:21.917
<i>That no one else</i>

1862
01:47:22.000 --> 01:47:25.583
<i>Feels like a betrayal after you</i>

1863
01:47:25.833 --> 01:47:29.458
<i>Might take a lifetime</i>

1864
01:47:29.667 --> 01:47:33.583
<i>For me</i>

1865
01:47:33.792 --> 01:47:36.750
<i>To forget you</i>

1866
01:47:37.667 --> 01:47:43.000
<i>Might take a lifetime for me</i>

1867
01:47:48.208 --> 01:47:49.768
Bani, you used to forget your
lines back then, too.

1868
01:47:49.792 --> 01:47:51.667
I miss that so much.

1869
01:47:51.750 --> 01:47:54.625
That fluttery feeling right before
stepping on stage.

1870
01:47:54.708 --> 01:47:55.708
Those jitters…

1871
01:47:56.167 --> 01:47:57.500
Can't feel that anymore.

1872
01:47:58.542 --> 01:47:59.542
Why not?

1873
01:48:01.625 --> 01:48:02.833
You can, if you want to.

1874
01:48:03.667 --> 01:48:04.907
Are you doing a play right now?

1875
01:48:05.875 --> 01:48:08.958
Yeah, I am. But I can't do it alone.

1876
01:48:10.167 --> 01:48:11.807
There's this brilliant part
in it for you.

1877
01:48:13.208 --> 01:48:15.500
If you do it,
I swear it's Oscar-worthy.

1878
01:48:15.958 --> 01:48:18.167
- An Oscar?
- Wow!

1879
01:48:18.250 --> 01:48:20.083
Okay.

1880
01:48:20.542 --> 01:48:21.542
So what's the part?

1881
01:48:26.958 --> 01:48:27.958
Stop.

1882
01:48:35.792 --> 01:48:37.250
Meet your new mom.

1883
01:48:37.542 --> 01:48:39.500
Shibani Ghosh Sarkar.

1884
01:48:39.792 --> 01:48:40.792
Hi.

1885
01:48:48.458 --> 01:48:49.458
Nice.

1886
01:48:50.833 --> 01:48:52.042
Where's our room?

1887
01:48:59.583 --> 01:49:02.000
Oh, big, nice room.

1888
01:49:02.292 --> 01:49:03.417
Hey, what's your name?

1889
01:49:03.792 --> 01:49:05.232
Whatever, whose room is this anyway?

1890
01:49:05.958 --> 01:49:08.250
- Mine.
- You're alone, and there are two of us.

1891
01:49:08.708 --> 01:49:10.500
Put my bag here.
We'll take this room.

1892
01:49:10.667 --> 01:49:11.667
Go on.

1893
01:49:17.042 --> 01:49:19.000
I'm feeling so bad.
She's such a sweet kid.

1894
01:49:19.083 --> 01:49:20.750
Don't say that, please.

1895
01:49:20.875 --> 01:49:21.958
Okay, okay.

1896
01:49:23.375 --> 01:49:25.208
Pari, aren't you going to join me?

1897
01:49:35.417 --> 01:49:36.708
How can you be so cruel?

1898
01:49:37.167 --> 01:49:38.375
She was nearly in tears.

1899
01:49:39.500 --> 01:49:40.500
That's the point.

1900
01:49:41.500 --> 01:49:44.708
I want her to cry, get mad, hate me…

1901
01:49:45.833 --> 01:49:46.833
And then leave.

1902
01:49:52.167 --> 01:49:54.667
- He didn't even know it was you?
- Nope.

1903
01:49:54.750 --> 01:49:57.333
Then I stripped him almost naked,

1904
01:49:58.625 --> 01:50:00.458
took his clothes,

1905
01:50:00.875 --> 01:50:03.500
- and left him in the hotel corridor.
- Wow.

1906
01:50:03.792 --> 01:50:04.958
What's your story?

1907
01:50:05.583 --> 01:50:07.917
Your girlfriend dumped you?
Ditched you?

1908
01:50:08.375 --> 01:50:09.375
Bang on.

1909
01:50:09.542 --> 01:50:10.667
What? Where?

1910
01:50:11.792 --> 01:50:13.333
Where did she go? She went up.

1911
01:50:14.375 --> 01:50:15.375
What?

1912
01:50:16.333 --> 01:50:17.333
She's dead.

1913
01:50:18.958 --> 01:50:19.958
That's a new one.

1914
01:50:20.000 --> 01:50:21.875
You mean dead to you, right?

1915
01:50:22.000 --> 01:50:23.375
No, like dead, dead.

1916
01:50:24.250 --> 01:50:26.417
Oh shit, I'm so sorry.

1917
01:50:28.542 --> 01:50:29.750
What was her name?

1918
01:50:30.250 --> 01:50:31.708
- Ria.
- What?

1919
01:50:32.833 --> 01:50:35.167
Ria!

1920
01:50:35.542 --> 01:50:37.083
Ria!

1921
01:50:37.208 --> 01:50:39.250
Life is shit!

1922
01:50:39.458 --> 01:50:42.375
Shit!

1923
01:50:43.500 --> 01:50:45.958
All men are dogs!

1924
01:50:46.042 --> 01:50:49.375
Dogs!

1925
01:50:51.625 --> 01:50:54.083
The world's biggest idiot is…

1926
01:50:54.167 --> 01:50:57.750
Monty Sisodia! Sisodia! Sisodia!

1927
01:50:58.208 --> 01:50:59.458
Let's get out of here.

1928
01:51:00.000 --> 01:51:01.042
Okay.

1929
01:51:04.333 --> 01:51:05.875
Gemini, my phone is stolen.

1930
01:51:06.250 --> 01:51:07.250
How to find it?

1931
01:51:07.375 --> 01:51:08.750
<i>To find your stolen phone,</i>

1932
01:51:08.958 --> 01:51:12.500
<i>download the Find My Device app
and enter your details.</i>

1933
01:51:13.875 --> 01:51:16.792
No, Baba likes green tea in the morning.

1934
01:51:16.958 --> 01:51:18.875
If he drinks milk tea,
he gets acidity.

1935
01:51:18.958 --> 01:51:22.958
My, my, you say it like he's always lived

1936
01:51:23.333 --> 01:51:24.792
with you and never with me.

1937
01:51:25.625 --> 01:51:31.958
I've always given him strong,
milky tea with sugar.

1938
01:51:32.125 --> 01:51:34.250
He never complained about acidity.

1939
01:51:35.000 --> 01:51:35.875
Throw it away.

1940
01:51:35.958 --> 01:51:37.958
- Slow down, please.
- Oh yes.

1941
01:51:38.458 --> 01:51:40.125
Hey. What was your name?

1942
01:51:40.667 --> 01:51:41.667
Doesn't matter.

1943
01:51:41.792 --> 01:51:45.333
Tomorrow morning, be up early
and start working in the kitchen.

1944
01:51:45.500 --> 01:51:47.542
I didn't come here to be a maid.

1945
01:51:48.667 --> 01:51:49.917
Can I ask you something?

1946
01:51:52.958 --> 01:51:54.583
How long have you two
known each other?

1947
01:51:55.958 --> 01:51:57.417
About seven years now.

1948
01:51:58.167 --> 01:51:59.625
One of his friends was a regular.

1949
01:52:00.542 --> 01:52:01.875
Regular?

1950
01:52:02.167 --> 01:52:04.042
My regular client.

1951
01:52:04.625 --> 01:52:06.542
That's how I met Parimal.

1952
01:52:07.125 --> 01:52:10.042
Since then,
he's been my only regular client.

1953
01:52:10.833 --> 01:52:13.417
Others came once in a while.

1954
01:52:13.750 --> 01:52:16.083
But he never missed a single day.

1955
01:52:16.250 --> 01:52:20.875
Who else comes to people like
us for entertainment at this age?

1956
01:52:26.708 --> 01:52:28.208
When his wife passed away…

1957
01:52:28.958 --> 01:52:30.667
I did feel bad for him.

1958
01:52:31.375 --> 01:52:32.708
But selfishly, I was happy too.

1959
01:52:33.000 --> 01:52:36.792
I thought he'd come to meet me
daily instead of weekly.

1960
01:52:37.750 --> 01:52:39.542
I even hoped he might marry me!

1961
01:52:40.792 --> 01:52:43.750
But he made me wait five years.

1962
01:52:44.625 --> 01:52:45.625
You know why?

1963
01:52:45.708 --> 01:52:46.875
Because of you!

1964
01:52:54.917 --> 01:52:57.542
I was going to call you.

1965
01:52:57.833 --> 01:52:59.375
<i>Ma, call Baba once.</i>

1966
01:52:59.500 --> 01:53:00.958
<i>He is really worried.</i>

1967
01:53:01.375 --> 01:53:03.000
Hi! Hi, Ma!

1968
01:53:03.083 --> 01:53:04.167
- Hi, how's Goa?
- Hi.

1969
01:53:04.292 --> 01:53:05.583
Oh, Goa's great.

1970
01:53:05.833 --> 01:53:08.083
Why are you wearing rollers?

1971
01:53:09.042 --> 01:53:10.458
Sis, your hair looks nice.

1972
01:53:10.625 --> 01:53:11.500
Really?

1973
01:53:11.583 --> 01:53:12.583
I don't know.

1974
01:53:13.917 --> 01:53:15.184
You sorted things out
with your husband?

1975
01:53:15.208 --> 01:53:17.833
- Well, it's…
- Hey, Maya, your helmet.

1976
01:53:17.958 --> 01:53:19.458
- Oh, thank you.
- Yeah.

1977
01:53:20.167 --> 01:53:21.333
I'm coming.

1978
01:53:21.708 --> 01:53:23.667
- Maya?
- I have been waiting for a long time.

1979
01:53:23.750 --> 01:53:24.750
I'll tell you later.

1980
01:53:24.792 --> 01:53:26.625
This is… this is Parimal.

1981
01:53:26.708 --> 01:53:30.292
Parimal, that's Chumki
and that's my eldest, Kajol.

1982
01:53:31.083 --> 01:53:32.583
- Hi.
- Hello.

1983
01:53:32.667 --> 01:53:33.875
Bye.

1984
01:53:34.083 --> 01:53:35.667
Listen, we need to leave.

1985
01:53:35.750 --> 01:53:36.667
Okay.

1986
01:53:36.750 --> 01:53:38.250
Okay, Ma, I have to go.

1987
01:53:38.333 --> 01:53:39.792
Chumki, bye. Talk to you later.

1988
01:53:39.875 --> 01:53:41.000
- Bye!
- Bye!

1989
01:53:42.375 --> 01:53:43.417
Bye.

1990
01:53:48.917 --> 01:53:51.125
Hey, what are you doing
over here by yourself?

1991
01:53:54.750 --> 01:53:56.042
I've got my eyes on you.

1992
01:53:57.083 --> 01:53:58.167
Stay off the phone.

1993
01:54:01.000 --> 01:54:03.333
What a total creep!
Such a damn pervert.

1994
01:54:05.000 --> 01:54:08.500
I swear, I just want to smack him.

1995
01:54:09.500 --> 01:54:11.250
You really should've
told people about us.

1996
01:54:12.542 --> 01:54:14.333
Have you completely lost it, babe?

1997
01:54:14.958 --> 01:54:16.875
If we tell him…

1998
01:54:16.958 --> 01:54:18.958
Maybe he'll stop touching me
all the time?

1999
01:54:20.000 --> 01:54:21.841
Come on, everyone knows
he has a thing for you.

2000
01:54:22.208 --> 01:54:23.208
Correct?

2001
01:54:23.542 --> 01:54:25.708
If he finds out we're engaged,

2002
01:54:26.500 --> 01:54:28.301
who do you think he's going
to take it out on?

2003
01:54:28.667 --> 01:54:29.708
Me, that's who.

2004
01:54:29.792 --> 01:54:31.333
Just three more months, babe.

2005
01:54:31.583 --> 01:54:33.417
I'll get my promotion,
and he'll be gone.

2006
01:54:40.708 --> 01:54:42.833
Theater's got a fix for everything.

2007
